    '14188_homeschool_discipleship_kit_files', 'CIVIL_PROCEDURE', 'Pretrial Procedures', 'E-Discovery',
    'Ruth, who leads a small homeschool co-op, sued Legacy Faith Resources, a Christian publishing house, in federal court after she suffered injuries while using one of the house''s Heritage Family Discipleship Kits. Jurisdiction was based on diversity. The co-op had purchased the kit for family and small-group Bible study and worship use. Ruth asked Legacy Faith Resources to produce "all electronically stored documents regarding the publishing house''s advertising strategy between 2008 and 2015, concerning the Heritage Family Discipleship Kits manufactured and sold by Legacy Faith Resources." In response, the publishing house offered to turn over all its advertising files for the years in question. The publishing house explained that all its documents pertaining to advertising are filed chronologically, without regard to the product line. Legacy Faith Resources produces at least 22 distinct product lines, including VBS kits, adult Bible studies, worship music resources, apparel, mission-prep guides, and others. Ruth moved to compel the production of only the advertising files she originally requested. Should the district court grant Ruth''s motion to compel?', 'Ruth, who leads a small homeschool co-op, sued Legacy Faith Resources, a Christian publishing house, in federal court after she suffered injuries while using one of the house''s Heritage Family Discipleship Kits. Jurisdiction was based on diversity. The co-op had purchased the kit for family and small-group Bible study and worship use. Ruth asked Legacy Faith Resources to produce "all electronically stored documents regarding the publishing house''s advertising strategy between 2008 and 2015, concerning the Heritage Family Discipleship Kits manufactured and sold by Legacy Faith Resources." In response, the publishing house offered to turn over all its advertising files for the years in question. The publishing house explained that all its documents pertaining to advertising are filed chronologically, withou