    '17117_day_school_playground_jmol', 'CIVIL_PROCEDURE', 'JMOL and Trial Motions', 'Rule 50(b) renewed JMOL — preservation of grounds from Rule 50(a)',
    'Mary runs a small Christian day school. She hired Paul, a playground-equipment contractor, to build a new playground on the school grounds for $32,000. Six weeks after completion, a five-year-old child broke her arm when a climber panel gave way. Mary sued Paul in federal district court on diversity grounds, asserting negligence and breach of warranty and seeking $40,000 in damages. Before the case was submitted to the jury, Paul moved for judgment as a matter of law under Rule 50(a) on the single ground that the $40,000 damages figure was not supported by the evidence. The court denied the motion. The jury returned a verdict for Mary and awarded $40,000. After the verdict, Paul filed a renewed motion for judgment as a matter of law under Rule 50(b) — his first time challenging causation — arguing that Mary had failed to introduce legally sufficient evidence that the climber''s failure caused the child''s broken arm.', 'Mary runs a small Christian day school. She hired Paul, a playground-equipment contractor, to build a new playground on the school grounds for $32,000. Six weeks after completion, a five-year-old child broke her arm when a climber panel gave way. Mary sued Paul in federal district court on diversity grounds, asserting negligence and breach of warranty and seeking $40,000 in damages. Before the case was submitted to the jury, Paul moved for judgment as a matter of law under Rule 50(a) on the single ground that the $40,000 damages figure was not supported by the evidence. The court denied the motion. The jury returned a verdict for Mary and awarded $40,000. After the verdict, Paul filed a renewed motion for judgment as a matter of law under Rule 50(b) — his first time challenging causation — arguing that Mary had failed to introduce legally sufficient evidence that the climber''s failure caused the child''s broken arm.', 'May the court grant the renewed Rule 50(b) motion on the new causation ground?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "17117", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "92080202", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
