) VALUES (
    '17913_summit_klaxon', 'CIVIL_PROCEDURE', 'Erie Doctrine and Choice of Law', 'Contract Choice Clause in Diversity',
    'Mary, a worship-summit organizer in State A, signed a written speaker agreement with Paul, a Christian conference speaker based in State C, for Paul to deliver the Friday-evening keynote at Mary''s summer worship summit in State A. The agreement contains a clause that states:

> "This agreement shall be governed by the laws of State C, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles."

State A''s choice-of-law rules enforce some contractual choice-of-law clauses but refuse to enforce others when the chosen state has no substantial relationship to the dispute. Paul later cancels the engagement, and Mary sues Paul for breach of contract in federal district court sitting in State A on the basis of diversity jurisdiction.', 'Mary, a worship-summit organizer in State A, signed a written speaker agreement with Paul, a Christian conference speaker based in State C, for Paul to deliver the Friday-evening keynote at Mary''s summer worship summit in State A. The agreement contains a clause that states:

> "This agreement shall be governed by the laws of State C, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles."

State A''s choice-of-law rules enforce some contractual choice-of-law clauses but refuse to enforce others when the chosen state has no substantial relationship to the dispute. Paul later cancels the engagement, and Mary sues Paul for breach of contract in federal district court sitting in State A on the basis of diversity jurisdiction.', 'How should the federal court decide whether State C law governs Mary''s claim?',
