SELECT q.question_id, 'C', 'Yes, because likely recovery below $75,000 defeats jurisdiction.', 0,
       '["misstated_rule", "bar_exam_bait", "common_student_myth"]', '["fabricated_rule"]', 'The student confuses the legal-certainty test with a probability-of-recovery test. The amount-in-controversy requirement is jurisdictional, but the jurisdictional inquiry is governed by what the plaintiff pleaded in good faith and what the law (statutes and contracts) makes legally possible — not by what either party predicts discovery will reveal. The Gold Key resolves: ''legal certainty'' means a fact that the law makes impossible, not a party''s prediction.',
