    '20567_psalm_panels_venue', 'CIVIL_PROCEDURE', 'Erie Doctrine and Choice of Law', 'Federal Statute Directly Controls',
    'Mary, a citizen of State Jordan, runs a private business that rents hand-painted “Psalms & Parables” stage panels for paid community programs. She sued Barnabas, a citizen of State Carmel, in the U.S. District Court for the Northern District of State Carmel for breach of a paid restoration contract involving those panels. A State Carmel statute provides that a civil action may be filed only in the county where the defendant resides. Barnabas resides in a county located in the Southern District of State Carmel. Federal venue statute § 1391 provides that venue is proper in a federal district where a substantial part of the events or omissions giving rise to the claim occurred. The design meetings, payment, restoration work, and disputed delivery all occurred in the Northern District.', 'Mary, a citizen of State Jordan, runs a private business that rents hand-painted “Psalms & Parables” stage panels for paid community programs. She sued Barnabas, a citizen of State Carmel, in the U.S. District Court for the Northern District of State Carmel for breach of a paid restoration contract involving those panels. A State Carmel statute provides that a civil action may be filed only in the county where the defendant resides. Barnabas resides in a county located in the Southern District of State Carmel. Federal venue statute § 1391 provides that venue is proper in a federal district where a substantial part of the events or omissions giving rise to the claim occurred. The design meetings, payment, restoration work, and disputed delivery all occurred in the Northern District.', 'Which venue rule should the federal court apply?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "20567", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "96060100", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
