    '22823_cedar_harp_restoration', 'CIVIL_PROCEDURE', 'Law Applied by Federal Courts (Erie)', 'State Law Applied in Federal Courts',
    'Mary hired Daniel, a Christian luthier, to restore her cedar harp for a home concert. Their one-page service contract said Daniel would “restore the harp and repair any broken parts needed for performance.” Mary paid half up front. After delivery, Mary said the contract required a new soundboard and an inlaid panel; Daniel said he promised only to refinish the frame, replace loose pegs, and restring the instrument. They sued in federal court on diversity grounds.

The judge held a bench trial. Mary and Daniel were the only witnesses, and they sharply disagreed about the scope of work promised in the contract. At the end of trial, the judge stated findings of fact on the record: Daniel had promised only the refinish, loose-peg, and string work, not a new soundboard or inlaid panel. Neither party objected to those findings. The judge entered judgment for Daniel. Mary appealed, arguing that the findings should be overturned. Is the appellate court likely to overturn the findings?', 'Mary hired Daniel, a Christian luthier, to restore her cedar harp for a home concert. Their one-page service contract said Daniel would “restore the harp and repair any broken parts needed for performance.” Mary paid half up front. After delivery, Mary said the contract required a new soundboard and an inlaid panel; Daniel said he promised only to refinish the frame, replace loose pegs, and restring the instrument. They sued in federal court on diversity grounds.

The judge held a bench trial. Mary and Daniel were the only witnesses, and they sharply disagreed about the scope of work promised in the contract. At the end of trial, the judge stated findings of fact on the record: Daniel had promised only the refinish, loose-peg, and string work, not a new soundboard or inlaid panel. Neither party objected to those findings. The judge entered judgment for Daniel. Mary appealed, arguing that the findings should be overturned. Is the appellate court likely to overturn the findings?', 'Is the appellate court likely to overturn the findings?',
