At a hearing before the Commission, the only evidence against Timothy consisted of written, signed statements from unnamed informants — none of whom were present or available for questioning. The statements asserted that each informant had purchased methamphetamine from Timothy at his tutoring office. Based solely on these statements, the Commission found that Timothy used his place of business for an illegal purpose and ordered his license revoked.

