    '14229_daily-bread-depot', 'CONSTITUTIONAL_LAW', 'Individual Rights', 'Eminent domain--Takings Clause',
    'Daniel owned a for-profit bakery and kitchen-supply shop called Daily Bread Depot. The shop''s building sat in the middle of a three-acre paved lot used entirely for customer parking and curbside pickup. Daniel applied for a building permit to add a paid demonstration kitchen for bread-baking classes. The proposed addition would equal 25% of the existing building. Berea city officials refused to issue the permit unless Daniel set aside, inside the business, an after-school homework room occupying floor space at least equal to the proposed demonstration-kitchen addition. The condition was authorized by the city''s zoning ordinance. Daniel filed suit in state court against the appropriate city officials, challenging the homework-room condition solely on constitutional grounds. The trial court upheld the condition even though the officials presented no evidence and made no findings to justify it other than a general assertion that supervised homework space was in short supply in the city. Daniel appealed.', 'Daniel owned a for-profit bakery and kitchen-supply shop called Daily Bread Depot. The shop''s building sat in the middle of a three-acre paved lot used entirely for customer parking and curbside pickup. Daniel applied for a building permit to add a paid demonstration kitchen for bread-baking classes. The proposed addition would equal 25% of the existing building. Berea city officials refused to issue the permit unless Daniel set aside, inside the business, an after-school homework room occupying floor space at least equal to the proposed demonstration-kitchen addition. The condition was authorized by the city''s zoning ordinance. Daniel filed suit in state court against the appropriate city officials, challenging the homework-room condition solely on constitutional grounds. The trial court upheld the condition even though the officials presented no evidence and made no findings to justify it other than a general assertion that supervised homework space was in short supply in the city. Daniel appealed.', 'The court hearing the appeal should hold that the condition imposed by the city on issuance of the building permit is',
