    'Congress passed a law requiring U.S. diplomatic envoys stationed abroad to deliver formal written protests to the governments of host nations whenever those nations violate international agreements on the sale of military equipment. The President believes quiet diplomacy is more effective with certain allies and has instructed the envoys not to deliver the protests. Is the President''s instruction constitutional?

