    '17540_good_samaritan_lantern_vapor', 'CONSTITUTIONAL_LAW', 'Interbranch Checks and Balances', 'Separation of Powers',
    'A sealant used to waterproof lantern batteries for military disaster-response kits gives off a fine vapor in component workshops. Long exposure to the vapor can damage workers'' lungs. Congress enacts the Safe Workshop Air Act, which bars operation of any workshop making those components when vapor levels exceed stated federal limits. The Act also creates an Agency, authorizes it to inspect covered workshops, and empowers it to issue Closure Orders, enforceable by the Department of Justice, directing any noncomplying workshop to close. Section 18 of the Act provides that a Closure Order does not become effective until 10 days after the Senate Readiness Committee approves it. After finding that vapor levels in a workshop operated by Lydia''s Good Samaritan Lantern Works exceed the Act''s limits, the Agency issues a Closure Order and sends copies to the Department of Justice and the Senate Readiness Committee as required by the Act. The Senate Readiness Committee refuses to approve the Closure Order.', 'A sealant used to waterproof lantern batteries for military disaster-response kits gives off a fine vapor in component workshops. Long exposure to the vapor can damage workers'' lungs. Congress enacts the Safe Workshop Air Act, which bars operation of any workshop making those components when vapor levels exceed stated federal limits. The Act also creates an Agency, authorizes it to inspect covered workshops, and empowers it to issue Closure Orders, enforceable by the Department of Justice, directing any noncomplying workshop to close. Section 18 of the Act provides that a Closure Order does not become effective until 10 days after the Senate Readiness Committee approves it. After finding that vapor levels in a workshop operated by Lydia''s Good Samaritan Lantern Works exceed the Act''s limits, the Agency issues a Closure Order and sends copies to the Department of Justice and the Senate Readiness Committee as required by the Act. The Senate Readiness Committee refuses to approve the Closure Order.', 'If the Department of Justice challenges the constitutionality of Section 18 in an appropriate proceeding, the court should find Section 18',
