    'A city fire-and-rescue department runs a cadet academy for firefighter and emergency-dispatch jobs. Daniel applied for a cadet position and was not selected. Daniel sued the department, alleging that he was passed over because he was of Korean heritage and that a less-qualified white applicant was selected instead.

The court ruled for Daniel, finding that the department had a long history of discriminating against applicants of Korean heritage. Under a consent decree, the department agreed to hire four employees of Korean heritage over the next two years and to select a person of Korean heritage for an open training-captain position.

