    '14382_bethlehem_lanterns', 'CONTRACTS', 'Contract Content and Meaning', 'Parol Evidence Rule / Usage of Trade',
    'Peter’s Pilgrim Supply, a private regional distributor that sells Christian craft goods to bookstores and camp stores, signed a written agreement with Lydia Lantern Works. Under the agreement, Peter’s would distribute Lydia’s “Bethlehem Star” devotional lantern kits for four years throughout an eleven-town river district. The agreement required Peter’s to “promote in good faith the sale of Bethlehem Star lantern kits” in that district, but it said nothing about whether Peter’s could distribute other devotional lantern kits. Nine months later, Peter’s agreed with Barnabas Bright Crafts to distribute Barnabas’s battery-free devotional lantern kits in the same eleven-town district.', 'Peter’s Pilgrim Supply, a private regional distributor that sells Christian craft goods to bookstores and camp stores, signed a written agreement with Lydia Lantern Works. Under the agreement, Peter’s would distribute Lydia’s “Bethlehem Star” devotional lantern kits for four years throughout an eleven-town river district. The agreement required Peter’s to “promote in good faith the sale of Bethlehem Star lantern kits” in that district, but it said nothing about whether Peter’s could distribute other devotional lantern kits. Nine months later, Peter’s agreed with Barnabas Bright Crafts to distribute Barnabas’s battery-free devotional lantern kits in the same eleven-town district.', 'If Lydia Lantern Works sues Peter’s Pilgrim Supply for breach of their distribution contract, which of the following facts, if established, would most strengthen Lydia’s case?',
