) VALUES (
    '14391_noble_fir_nativity', 'CONTRACTS', 'Defenses to Enforceability', 'Supervening impracticability / illegality (mistake as alternative theory)',
    'Mary chairs the Living Nativity committee at a church in California and on May 20 wrote to several wholesale evergreen nurseries asking about 100 noble firs for the church''s annual outdoor Nativity scene. On June 1, she received the following signed letter from a wholesale tree farm in Oregon run by Paul:

> "We have just obtained 100 of the noble firs you inquired about and can supply them for $180 each. We can guarantee shipment no later than August 1."

On June 10, Paul sold and delivered the same firs to another church for $215 each. Unaware of that transaction, Mary on the morning of June 11 mailed Paul a letter rejecting the offer, but, changing her mind an hour later, retrieved from her local post office the letter of rejection and immediately dispatched to Paul a letter of acceptance, which Paul received on June 14. On June 9, a valid federal Plant Protection Act quarantine order making the interstate shipment of noble firs from Oregon punishable as a federal crime had become effective, but neither Mary nor Paul was aware until June 15 that the quarantine was already in effect.', 'Mary chairs the Living Nativity committee at a church in California and on May 20 wrote to several wholesale evergreen nurseries asking about 100 noble firs for the church''s annual outdoor Nativity scene. On June 1, she received the following signed letter from a wholesale tree farm in Oregon run by Paul:

> "We have just obtained 100 of the noble firs you inquired about and can supply them for $180 each. We can guarantee shipment no later than August 1."

On June 10, Paul sold and delivered the same firs to another church for $215 each. Unaware of that transaction, Mary on the morning of June 11 mailed Paul a letter rejecting the offer, but, changing her mind an hour later, retrieved from her local post office the letter of rejection and immediately dispatched to Paul a letter of acceptance, which Paul received on June 14. On June 9, a valid federal Plant Protection Act quarantine order making the interstate shipment of noble firs from Oregon punishable as a federal crime had become effective, but neither Mary nor Paul was aware until June 15 that the quarantine was already in effect.', 'As between Mary and Paul, which of the following is an accurate statement?',
