    'Daniel runs a private Jonah-themed escape-room booth for Christian conventions. He called Lydia, a wholesaler of ordinary catalog-stock olivewood fish keychains, and said that he would buy 800 keychains for his booth if Lydia could get them to him within seven days. Daniel did not mention a price. At the time of the call, the market price for 800 of those keychains was about $9,600. Lydia did not say yes or no on the call. Six days later, her driver arrived at Daniel''s storage unit with the 800 keychains and an invoice for $9,600. Before the driver arrived, the convention organizer had canceled Daniel''s booth space. Daniel refused to receive the keychains or pay the invoice.', 'Daniel runs a private Jonah-themed escape-room booth for Christian conventions. He called Lydia, a wholesaler of ordinary catalog-stock olivewood fish keychains, and said that he would buy 800 keychains for his booth if Lydia could get them to him within seven days. Daniel did not mention a price. At the time of the call, the market price for 800 of those keychains was about $9,600. Lydia did not say yes or no on the call. Six days later, her driver arrived at Daniel''s storage unit with the 800 keychains and an invoice for $9,600. Before the driver arrived, the convention organizer had canceled Daniel''s booth space. Daniel refused to receive the keychains or pay the invoice.', 'Is there an enforceable contract between Daniel and Lydia?',
