    '14409_sunken_ark_hall', 'CONTRACTS', 'Formation of Contracts', 'Assumption of risk for unknown subsurface conditions',
    'Lydia owned a private, for-profit Christian family camp called Mustard Seed Adventures. For an agreed price of $8 million, Barnabas Construction, a company specializing in large themed projects and excavation, contracted to design and build on Lydia’s lakeside parcel a Noah’s-Ark-shaped indoor climbing hall. Because sinkholes were common in the area, a local safety ordinance required the hall’s foundation and underground utilities to be excavated at least 18 feet.

Barnabas began digging and, at 11 feet, encountered a continuous shelf of limestone. When the contract was made, neither Lydia nor Barnabas knew of the limestone, and neither had hired a geotechnical expert to test for subsurface rock. Barnabas accurately claimed that removing enough limestone to build as planned would cost an additional $1.2 million and would probably leave it with a net loss of $800,000 on the job. Barnabas refused to continue unless Lydia promised to pay an additional $1 million for the completed hall.', 'Lydia owned a private, for-profit Christian family camp called Mustard Seed Adventures. For an agreed price of $8 million, Barnabas Construction, a company specializing in large themed projects and excavation, contracted to design and build on Lydia’s lakeside parcel a Noah’s-Ark-shaped indoor climbing hall. Because sinkholes were common in the area, a local safety ordinance required the hall’s foundation and underground utilities to be excavated at least 18 feet.

Barnabas began digging and, at 11 feet, encountered a continuous shelf of limestone. When the contract was made, neither Lydia nor Barnabas knew of the limestone, and neither had hired a geotechnical expert to test for subsurface rock. Barnabas accurately claimed that removing enough limestone to build as planned would cost an additional $1.2 million and would probably leave it with a net loss of $800,000 on the job. Barnabas refused to continue unless Lydia promised to pay an additional $1 million for the completed hall.', 'If Lydia refuses and sues Barnabas for breach of contract, which of the following will the court probably decide?',
