    '14425_accommodating-shipment', 'CONTRACTS', 'Formation of Contracts', 'Offer',
    'Barnabas runs a small woodworking shop and regularly buys hardwood planks from Timothy, a lumber supplier he has worked with for years. On Monday morning, Barnabas texts Timothy: "Need 50 board-feet of oak, delivered by end of week, at your usual price of $200." Timothy''s Oak Barn is temporarily out of oak. On Tuesday, Timothy delivers 50 board-feet of maple to Barnabas''s shop and includes this note with the delivery: "Oak is back-ordered. Maple is what I have on hand — sending you 50 board-feet at the same price of $200. Hope it works for your project." Barnabas receives both the maple shipment and the note on Tuesday afternoon.', 'Barnabas runs a small woodworking shop and regularly buys hardwood planks from Timothy, a lumber supplier he has worked with for years. On Monday morning, Barnabas texts Timothy: "Need 50 board-feet of oak, delivered by end of week, at your usual price of $200." Timothy''s Oak Barn is temporarily out of oak. On Tuesday, Timothy delivers 50 board-feet of maple to Barnabas''s shop and includes this note with the delivery: "Oak is back-ordered. Maple is what I have on hand — sending you 50 board-feet at the same price of $200. Hope it works for your project." Barnabas receives both the maple shipment and the note on Tuesday afternoon.', 'Which of the following best describes the rights and duties of Barnabas and Timothy?',
