    '14462_mustard_seed_carts', 'CONTRACTS', 'Performance, Breach, and Discharge', 'Conditions / waiver of condition',
    'Lydia Learning LLC, a private company that runs Bible-verse calligraphy camps, agreed in writing to buy from Ruth twelve hand-painted mobile coffee carts branded for ''Mustard Seed Morning'' events at a fixed price per cart. Lydia Learning was a subsidiary of Emmaus Market Group. Just before the written contract was signed, Martha, Lydia Learning''s purchasing director, said to Ruth, ''Of course, our commitment to buy is subject to approval from Emmaus Market Group.'' Ruth replied, ''Fine. No problem.'' Ruth later refused to deliver the carts, arguing that Lydia Learning had never asked Emmaus Market Group to approve the contract. That was true. Barnabas, the chief executive officer of Emmaus Market Group, is prepared to testify that Emmaus Market Group would have routinely approved the contract if asked. Lydia Learning can also prove that it sold a delivery van to raise money for the coffee-cart purchase, although it admits that it had not anticipated any need to sell the van when it entered the contract.', 'Lydia Learning LLC, a private company that runs Bible-verse calligraphy camps, agreed in writing to buy from Ruth twelve hand-painted mobile coffee carts branded for ''Mustard Seed Morning'' events at a fixed price per cart. Lydia Learning was a subsidiary of Emmaus Market Group. Just before the written contract was signed, Martha, Lydia Learning''s purchasing director, said to Ruth, ''Of course, our commitment to buy is subject to approval from Emmaus Market Group.'' Ruth replied, ''Fine. No problem.'' Ruth later refused to deliver the carts, arguing that Lydia Learning had never asked Emmaus Market Group to approve the contract. That was true. Barnabas, the chief executive officer of Emmaus Market Group, is prepared to testify that Emmaus Market Group would have routinely approved the contract if asked. Lydia Learning can also prove that it sold a delivery van to raise money for the coffee-cart purchase, although it admits that it had not anticipated any