    'Paul contracted in a signed writing to sell Lydia''s private Christian retreat-supply business 1,200 cedar fish ornaments each week for eight weeks, the ornaments to be delivered to Lydia''s warehouse on Thursdays and payment to be made on Mondays of each week. Lydia''s business packed all of its weekly Scripture craft kits on Fridays. On Thursday morning of the first week, Paul tendered delivery of 960 ornaments to Lydia, and Lydia accepted them on Paul''s assurance that the remaining 240 ornaments would be delivered later that evening, which they were. Lydia paid for both deliveries on Monday. On Thursday of the second week, Paul tendered delivery of 600 ornaments to Lydia and said that the remaining 600 ornaments could not be delivered on Thursday but would be delivered by Saturday. Lydia rejected the tender. Was Lydia legally justified in rejecting the tender of the 600 ornaments?', 'Paul contracted in a signed writing to sell Lydia''s private Christian retreat-supply business 1,200 cedar fish ornaments each week for eight weeks, the ornaments to be delivered to Lydia''s warehouse on Thursdays and payment to be made on Mondays of each week. Lydia''s business packed all of its weekly Scripture craft kits on Fridays. On Thursday morning of the first week, Paul tendered delivery of 960 ornaments to Lydia, and Lydia accepted them on Paul''s assurance that the remaining 240 ornaments would be delivered later that evening, which they were. Lydia paid for both deliveries on Monday. On Thursday of the second week, Paul tendered delivery of 600 ornaments to Lydia and said that the remaining 600 ornaments could not be delivered on Thursday but would be delivered by Saturday. Lydia rejected the tender. Was Lydia legally justified in rejecting the tender of the 600 ornaments?', 'Was Lydia legally justified in rejecting the tender of the 600 ornaments?',
