    '14481_ruth_nativity_music_box', 'CONTRACTS', 'Performance, Breach, and Discharge', 'Impossibility',
    'On March 3, Ruth agreed in a signed writing to sell Stephen a one-of-a-kind hand-carved Nativity music box for $12,000. The music box belonged to Ruth personally and, when they signed, was on loan for display at a private Scripture-arts exhibit in another city. Ruth was to deliver the music box to Stephen on May 1. On April 10, before the risk of loss had passed to Stephen, an electrical fire at the exhibit completely destroyed the music box, without fault of either Ruth or Stephen. After the contract was signed but before the fire, collector demand had increased the music box''s value to $18,000. Ruth sued Stephen for the $12,000 contract price, and Stephen counterclaimed for $18,000.', 'On March 3, Ruth agreed in a signed writing to sell Stephen a one-of-a-kind hand-carved Nativity music box for $12,000. The music box belonged to Ruth personally and, when they signed, was on loan for display at a private Scripture-arts exhibit in another city. Ruth was to deliver the music box to Stephen on May 1. On April 10, before the risk of loss had passed to Stephen, an electrical fire at the exhibit completely destroyed the music box, without fault of either Ruth or Stephen. After the contract was signed but before the fire, collector demand had increased the music box''s value to $18,000. Ruth sued Stephen for the $12,000 contract price, and Stephen counterclaimed for $18,000.', 'What is the likely outcome of this suit?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "14481_ruth_nativity_music_box", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "56050601", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
