    'On January 10, Ruth and Paul signed a written contract for Ruth to sell, and Paul to buy, Ruth''s old bakery building and attached garden lot, all on one parcel, where Paul hoped to open a private Bible-verse calligraphy studio. The closing was scheduled for October 15. On March 4, Paul unequivocally repudiated the contract. On March 22, Ruth urged Paul to reconsider and still proceed with the October 15 closing. On July 30, after hearing nothing further from Paul, Ruth sold and conveyed the parcel to Naomi without notifying Paul. On October 15, Paul attempted to close under the January 10 contract by tendering the full purchase price to Ruth. Ruth rejected the tender.', 'On January 10, Ruth and Paul signed a written contract for Ruth to sell, and Paul to buy, Ruth''s old bakery building and attached garden lot, all on one parcel, where Paul hoped to open a private Bible-verse calligraphy studio. The closing was scheduled for October 15. On March 4, Paul unequivocally repudiated the contract. On March 22, Ruth urged Paul to reconsider and still proceed with the October 15 closing. On July 30, after hearing nothing further from Paul, Ruth sold and conveyed the parcel to Naomi without notifying Paul. On October 15, Paul attempted to close under the January 10 contract by tendering the full purchase price to Ruth. Ruth rejected the tender.', 'If Paul sues Ruth for breach of contract, Paul will probably',
