    'Ruth owned a private hymn-recording studio that was being renovated for a family worship album project. On February 6, Ruth entered into a contract with Timothy, an audio technician, to calibrate and test the studio''s microphone system. The contract expressly required Timothy to begin the calibration work on April 20 so that Lydia''s video crew could mount camera rails after the sound cables were labeled.

