    'Lydia operates a private craft workshop that sells devotional event supplies. In a signed writing, Lydia contracted with Daniel, who runs a private Bible-memory retreat, for the sale to Daniel of 40 identical Psalm 23 shadow-lantern kits. The writing called for 20 kits to be delivered on October 10 and the remaining 20 kits on October 24. The writing did not state the place of delivery or the time or place for payment. On October 10, Lydia tendered 19 kits and said, “One kit was crushed in the courier’s truck on its way from my supplier to me, but I will deliver a replacement within four days.”', 'Lydia operates a private craft workshop that sells devotional event supplies. In a signed writing, Lydia contracted with Daniel, who runs a private Bible-memory retreat, for the sale to Daniel of 40 identical Psalm 23 shadow-lantern kits. The writing called for 20 kits to be delivered on October 10 and the remaining 20 kits on October 24. The writing did not state the place of delivery or the time or place for payment. On October 10, Lydia tendered 19 kits and said, “One kit was crushed in the courier’s truck on its way from my supplier to me, but I will deliver a replacement within four days.”', 'Which statement is correct?',
