On April 30, Paul accepted a conveyance and possession of the barn and paid the $150,000 purchase price, but notified Peter that he was reserving any rights he might have to damages caused by Peter''s breach. Paul intended to use the studio to record a worship album and had scheduled a 15-day tracking block with musicians beginning April 15. Because he did not have possession of the barn on that date, he had to rent a mobile sound-recording trailer at a cost of $1,000 for the 15 days. Peter had no reason to know that Paul intended to use the barn as a worship-recording studio or that he had rented the mobile trailer.', 'In an action by Paul against Peter for damages, Paul is entitled to recover',
