Before the installation period began, and with enough time left for timely completion, Peter told Lydia that he had sold his rigging shop to Barnabas, who was equally skilled in suspending oversized art pieces, and that Barnabas had agreed to take over the Peter-Lydia contract.', 'Lydia owned a private Bible-library with a glass atrium and a painted Gospel mural. Peter, a specialist in suspending oversized Christian art, signed a written contract with Lydia to hoist and mount a heavy bronze dove-and-olive-branch chandelier in the atrium.

