    '20883_unilat-barnabas-garden', 'CONTRACTS', 'Formation of Contracts', 'Unilateral contract',
    'Barnabas owns a small orchard of olive trees that he tends behind his home. His neighbor Lydia has a larger grove whose trees are producing poorly. On April 1, Barnabas posted the following notice on the community board at the local grain market:

"I will pay $300 to any person who delivers to me, before July 1, a written plan for amending the soil in my neighbor Lydia''s grove that will significantly increase its olive yield. If more than one person submits a plan, I will pay the $300 to the person whose plan, in my judgment, can be carried out at the lowest cost."

Timothy, a farmworker in the village, read the notice on April 4. He began studying soil conditions in his spare time. On April 9, Timothy wrote the following note: "I accept your offer of $300 for preparing a soil amendment plan for Lydia''s grove. I am already working on it and expect to have my plan ready within two weeks." He handed the note to a messenger to deliver to Barnabas, but the messenger misplaced it and it never arrived.

**Answer choices (post-shuffle):**

A: an offer for a bilateral contract.

B: an offer for a unilateral contract that ripened into a bilateral contract when Timothy wrote the note on April 9 and gave it to the messenger.

C: a preliminary invitation to deal, analogous to a newspaper advertisement for the sale of goods.

D: an offer for a unilateral contract.', 'Barnabas owns a small orchard of olive trees that he tends behind his home. His neighbor Lydia has a larger grove whose trees are producing poorly. On April 1, Barnabas posted the following notice on the community board at the local grain market:

"I will pay $300 to any person who delivers to me, before July 1, a written plan for amending the soil in my neighbor Lydia''s grove that will significantly increase its olive yield. If more than one person submits a plan, I will pay the $300 to the person whose plan, in my judgment, can be carried out at the lowest cost."

