    difficulty, status, source_type, version, metadata
) VALUES (
    '21525_minor-tutor-laptop', 'CONTRACTS', 'Defenses to Enforceability', 'Lack of Capacity',
    'Timothy is a 17-year-old who looks older than his age. He wants a new laptop for his college-preparatory coursework. He goes to Lydia''s electronics shop and picks out a model she has on display. Timothy tells Lydia he wants a brand-new one still in the box. Lydia explains that the display unit is the only one in stock, but she can order a new one from her supplier. Timothy and Lydia sign a written agreement: Lydia will deliver a new laptop to Timothy in two weeks for $850, payable on delivery. The next day, Timothy orders a custom-fit protective sleeve and a wireless mouse for the laptop. One week later, Lydia calls Timothy and says the laptop has arrived, but she will not deliver it unless Timothy proves he is over 18 or brings an adult to co-sign. Timothy immediately sues Lydia for breach of contract. The court should find for

**A:** Lydia, because Timothy lacked contractual capacity.
**B:** Lydia, because if she delivers the laptop, Timothy might later disaffirm the contract and demand his money back.
**C:** Timothy, because one who contracts with a minor is obligated to perform.
**D:** Timothy, because he bought a protective sleeve and wireless mouse in justified reliance on Lydia''s promise.', 'Timothy is a 17-year-old who looks older than his age. He wants a new laptop for his college-preparatory coursework. He goes to Lydia''s electronics shop and picks out a model she has on display. Timothy tells Lydia he wants a brand-new one still in the box. Lydia explains that the display unit is the only one in stock, but she can order a new one from her supplier. Timothy and Lydia sign a written agreement: Lydia will deliver a new laptop to Timothy in two weeks for $850, payable on delivery. The next day, Timothy orders a custom-fit protective sleeve and a wireless mouse for the laptop. One week later, Lydia calls Timothy and says the laptop has arrived, but she will not deliver it unless Timothy proves he is over 18 or brings an adult to co-sign. Timothy immediately sues Lydia for breach of contract. The court should find for

