    '22444_lighting_platform_rescue', 'CONTRACTS', 'Formation of Contracts', 'Consideration - past services and material benefit',
    'At a privately run Christian youth-theater studio, a lighting platform collapsed during rehearsal for a Bible-pageant scene. Lydia pulled Ruth, Naomi''s adult daughter, clear of the platform and kept her breathing until paramedics arrived. Ruth survived. After hearing what Lydia had done, Naomi signed a note that stated: "In consideration of Lydia''s saving Ruth''s life, I promise to pay Lydia $700." Naomi died six weeks after signing the note. Lydia submitted a $700 claim to the administrator of Naomi''s estate, but the administrator denied it.', 'At a privately run Christian youth-theater studio, a lighting platform collapsed during rehearsal for a Bible-pageant scene. Lydia pulled Ruth, Naomi''s adult daughter, clear of the platform and kept her breathing until paramedics arrived. Ruth survived. After hearing what Lydia had done, Naomi signed a note that stated: "In consideration of Lydia''s saving Ruth''s life, I promise to pay Lydia $700." Naomi died six weeks after signing the note. Lydia submitted a $700 claim to the administrator of Naomi''s estate, but the administrator denied it.', 'Is the fact that Lydia saved Ruth''s life sufficient consideration for Naomi''s promise to pay Lydia $700?',
