) VALUES (
    '22471_hymnbook_warehouse_reward', 'CONTRACTS', 'Formation > Consideration > Preexisting duty', 'Formation of Contracts',
    'Lydia and Barnabas own a private Christian recording studio that keeps a small display of family music artifacts in its lobby. After a concert, someone stole Lydia''s late grandmother''s handwritten hymnbook from a locked road case. Lydia and Barnabas posted a livestream announcement offering a $75,000 reward to anyone who identified the thief and returned the hymnbook.

A few days later, Daniel, an on-duty city police officer who had heard about the reward, received a tip from an informant that the thief was using a rented warehouse behind a closed print shop. Daniel watched the warehouse for several hours. Near midnight, he saw Stephen walk outside carrying the hymnbook. Daniel arrested Stephen and returned the hymnbook to Lydia and Barnabas. When Lydia thanked him, Daniel requested the reward. Lydia and Barnabas refused to pay. Daniel sued for the reward.', 'Lydia and Barnabas own a private Christian recording studio that keeps a small display of family music artifacts in its lobby. After a concert, someone stole Lydia''s late grandmother''s handwritten hymnbook from a locked road case. Lydia and Barnabas posted a livestream announcement offering a $75,000 reward to anyone who identified the thief and returned the hymnbook.

A few days later, Daniel, an on-duty city police officer who had heard about the reward, received a tip from an informant that the thief was using a rented warehouse behind a closed print shop. Daniel watched the warehouse for several hours. Near midnight, he saw Stephen walk outside carrying the hymnbook. Daniel arrested Stephen and returned the hymnbook to Lydia and Barnabas. When Lydia thanked him, Daniel requested the reward. Lydia and Barnabas refused to pay. Daniel sued for the reward.', 'Should the court rule for Daniel?',
