    'At a privately run Christian music camp, Stephen was on a rented scissor lift hanging a banner for Psalm Sing Night when the lift''s hydraulic arm jammed and left the platform angled over a gravel walkway. Stephen''s sister Mary stood below and screamed, "Lord, will somebody please get Stephen down?" Peter, who happened to have climbing gear in his truck, heard the cry, climbed the support frame, and brought Stephen safely down. Peter later asked Mary to pay him for his trouble, but Mary refused.', 'At a privately run Christian music camp, Stephen was on a rented scissor lift hanging a banner for Psalm Sing Night when the lift''s hydraulic arm jammed and left the platform angled over a gravel walkway. Stephen''s sister Mary stood below and screamed, "Lord, will somebody please get Stephen down?" Peter, who happened to have climbing gear in his truck, heard the cry, climbed the support frame, and brought Stephen safely down. Peter later asked Mary to pay him for his trouble, but Mary refused.', 'If Peter asserts a claim for payment against Mary on a theory of promissory estoppel, which of the following would be Mary''s most effective argument in defense?',
