) VALUES (
    '14560_death_qualified_choir', 'CRIMINAL', 'Constitutional Protection of Accused Persons', 'Death-qualified jury and fair-cross-section challenge',
    'Daniel was charged with capital first-degree murder after a fatal shooting outside a city-sponsored Christmas choir festival. The only available punishments were death or life in prison without parole. During jury selection, the trial judge, over Daniel''s objection, granted the prosecution''s for-cause challenges to five prospective jurors. Each juror said, after questioning by both sides, that he or she was personally opposed to the death penalty and was unsure whether he or she could ever vote to impose it.

The jury convicted Daniel and, after a separate sentencing hearing, sentenced him to death. On appeal, Daniel''s only argument is that excusing those prospective jurors violated his federal constitutional right to a jury chosen from a fair cross section of the community.', 'Daniel was charged with capital first-degree murder after a fatal shooting outside a city-sponsored Christmas choir festival. The only available punishments were death or life in prison without parole. During jury selection, the trial judge, over Daniel''s objection, granted the prosecution''s for-cause challenges to five prospective jurors. Each juror said, after questioning by both sides, that he or she was personally opposed to the death penalty and was unsure whether he or she could ever vote to impose it.

The jury convicted Daniel and, after a separate sentencing hearing, sentenced him to death. On appeal, Daniel''s only argument is that excusing those prospective jurors violated his federal constitutional right to a jury chosen from a fair cross section of the community.', 'How should the court of appeals rule on the conviction and the death sentence?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "14560_death_qualified_choir", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "75090500", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
