    '14573_psalm_maze_stole', 'CRIMINAL', 'Constitutional Protection of Accused Persons', 'Searches and Seizures',
    'Stephen, a traveling hymnal printer, had been missing for several months. The sheriff''s department received an anonymous tip that Lydia, who operated a private Scripture-verse sunflower maze, had buried Stephen near an irrigation berm about 250 yards from Lydia''s farmhouse.

Deputies went to Lydia''s rural property. They cut the chain on the deer fence surrounding the sunflower rows and entered, looking for the grave. They also searched nearby crop rows inside the same fence and discovered Stephen''s embroidered choir stole tied around a wooden row marker bearing a psalm verse.

Lydia saw the deputies find the stole and began shooting at them. The deputies returned fire. Lydia ran to her all-terrain vehicle to escape, but it would not start. She then fled across the field toward an equipment shed. Deputy Paul tackled Lydia just as she reached the shed. As Lydia tried to rise, Paul pinned her arms behind her back. Another deputy threatened, "Tell us what happened to Stephen or we will shut down the maze and make sure your family loses the farm." Lydia responded that she had killed Stephen during a fight but had not reported it because she did not want authorities entering the land and finding the illegal pesticide barrels she kept near the shed. She said she buried Stephen behind the shed.

Lydia is thereafter charged with murder. If Lydia moves to exclude the introduction of Stephen''s stole into evidence, the court should:', 'Stephen, a traveling hymnal printer, had been missing for several months. The sheriff''s department received an anonymous tip that Lydia, who operated a private Scripture-verse sunflower maze, had buried Stephen near an irrigation berm about 250 yards from Lydia''s farmhouse.

Deputies went to Lydia''s rural property. They cut the chain on the deer fence surrounding the sunflower rows and entered, looking for the grave. They also searched nearby crop rows inside the same fence and discovered Stephen''s embroidered choir stole tied around a wooden row marker bearing a psalm verse.

Lydia saw the deputies find the stole and began shooting at them. The deputies returned fire. Lydia ran to her all-terrain vehicle to escape, but it would not start. She then fled across the field toward an equipment shed. Deputy Paul tackled Lydia just as she reached the shed. As Lydia tried to rise, Paul pinned her arms behind her back. Another deputy threatened, "Tell us what happened to Stephen or we will shut down the maze and make sure your family loses the farm." Lydia responded that she had killed Stephen during a fight but had not reported it because she did not want authorities entering the land and finding the illegal pesticide barrels she kept near the shed. She said she buried Stephen behind the shed.

Lydia is thereafter charged with murder. If Lydia moves to exclude the introduction of Stephen''s stole into evidence, the court should:', 'If Lydia moves to exclude the introduction of Stephen''s stole into evidence, the court should:',
