> “Forcible seizure is taking a movable item from an unconsenting person by means of force or violence. Consent of the person is a complete defense to a charge of forcible seizure.”

During Daniel’s trial for forcible seizure, he testified that, at a gospel-festival rehearsal, Naomi consented to his taking her hand-painted psalm drum for the processional.', 'How should the trial judge instruct the jury regarding the burden of proof on the issue of consent?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "14588", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "75090500", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
