    '14591_toll-booth-fentanyl', 'CRIMINAL', 'Fourth Amendment', 'Arrest and Detention',
    'Ruth was driving home from a Christian women''s conference when a state trooper stopped her at a toll booth for an expired vehicle registration. One trooper approached Ruth''s car to issue a citation while the other remained in the patrol car and ran a computer check of Ruth''s license plate. The computer check indicated that there was an outstanding warrant for Ruth''s arrest for failure to pay child support. The troopers then arrested Ruth based on the warrant and proceeded to search her. During the search, they discovered a package of fentanyl in Ruth''s purse. Later, it was learned that Ruth had satisfied the child-support obligation 12 days earlier and that the warrant had been quashed, but the clerk of the court had failed to update the computer database, which continued to list the warrant as outstanding. Ruth was charged with unlawful possession of fentanyl. Her attorney has filed a motion to suppress the use of the fentanyl as evidence. Should the motion be granted?', 'Ruth was driving home from a Christian women''s conference when a state trooper stopped her at a toll booth for an expired vehicle registration. One trooper approached Ruth''s car to issue a citation while the other remained in the patrol car and ran a computer check of Ruth''s license plate. The computer check indicated that there was an outstanding warrant for Ruth''s arrest for failure to pay child support. The troopers then arrested Ruth based on the warrant and proceeded to search her. During the search, they discovered a package of fentanyl in Ruth''s purse. Later, it was learned that Ruth had satisfied the child-support obligation 12 days earlier and that the warrant had been quashed, but the clerk of the court had failed to update the computer database, which continued to list the warrant as outstanding. Ruth was charged with unlawful possession of fentanyl. Her attorney has filed a motion to suppress the use of the fentanyl as evidence. Should the motion be granted?', 'Should the motion be granted?',
