    '14670_brass_handbell_pageant', 'CRIMINAL', 'Mens rea', 'General Principles',
    'At a private Scripture-memory game night in Daniel''s rooftop studio, Peter accused Daniel of sending suggestive messages to Peter''s wife, Ruth. Peter and Ruth left the gathering. The next afternoon, at a rented rehearsal hall where volunteers were preparing a Christmas pageant, Daniel saw Peter, grabbed a heavy brass handbell from a props table, and struck Peter on the head. Peter fell into a coma and died 18 days later.

This jurisdiction defines aggravated assault as an assault with any weapon or dangerous implement and punishes it as a felony. It defines murder as the unlawful killing of a person with malice aforethought or in the course of an independent felony. Assume that the jury makes the following findings: Daniel did not act in a rage provoked by Peter''s accusation, Daniel intended either to kill Peter or to inflict serious bodily harm, and the killing occurred in the course of an aggravated assault.', 'At a private Scripture-memory game night in Daniel''s rooftop studio, Peter accused Daniel of sending suggestive messages to Peter''s wife, Ruth. Peter and Ruth left the gathering. The next afternoon, at a rented rehearsal hall where volunteers were preparing a Christmas pageant, Daniel saw Peter, grabbed a heavy brass handbell from a props table, and struck Peter on the head. Peter fell into a coma and died 18 days later.

This jurisdiction defines aggravated assault as an assault with any weapon or dangerous implement and punishes it as a felony. It defines murder as the unlawful killing of a person with malice aforethought or in the course of an independent felony. Assume that the jury makes the following findings: Daniel did not act in a rage provoked by Peter''s accusation, Daniel intended either to kill Peter or to inflict serious bodily harm, and the killing occurred in the course of an aggravated assault.', 'Daniel may be found guilty of murder',
