) VALUES (
    '14691_church-keyboard-heist', 'CRIMINAL', 'Inchoate Crimes', 'Conspiracy',
    'Stephen, a church music coordinator, learned that a vintage keyboard donated to Faithful Church could be removed through a side door left ajar by volunteers. He approached longtime choir member Martha and explained how she could enter the church after hours and carry the keyboard out. He did not tell her he was a church employee. Martha agreed to help him steal the keyboard and sell it. A church deacon overheard their conversation and reported it to police. Police arrested Stephen and Martha. Both were charged with conspiracy to commit theft. Before trial, Stephen claimed charitable immunity as a church officer and obtained dismissal of the charge against him. Martha then moved to dismiss the conspiracy charge against her. The jurisdiction has adopted the Model Penal Code version of conspiracy. Should the court grant Martha''s motion to dismiss the conspiracy charge against her?', 'Stephen, a church music coordinator, learned that a vintage keyboard donated to Faithful Church could be removed through a side door left ajar by volunteers. He approached longtime choir member Martha and explained how she could enter the church after hours and carry the keyboard out. He did not tell her he was a church employee. Martha agreed to help him steal the keyboard and sell it. A church deacon overheard their conversation and reported it to police. Police arrested Stephen and Martha. Both were charged with conspiracy to commit theft. Before trial, Stephen claimed charitable immunity as a church officer and obtained dismissal of the charge against him. Martha then moved to dismiss the conspiracy charge against her. The jurisdiction has adopted the Model Penal Code version of conspiracy. Should the court grant Martha''s motion to dismiss the conspiracy charge against her?', 'Should the court grant Martha''s motion to dismiss the conspiracy charge against her?',
