    'Ruth and her sister Lydia returned to the United States from a Scripture-art market in Belize. At U.S. Customs, officers found packets of fentanyl powder hidden under false bottoms in separate wooden hymnbook display boxes that each sister was carrying. Both sisters were arrested. During separate questioning, Ruth started crying and said, "I told Lydia this terminal had too many inspectors." Lydia gave no statement.

