    '16012_stolen-flock', 'CRIMINAL', 'Constitutional Protection of Accused Persons', 'Identifications',
    'Stephen had been arraigned on a charge of stealing sheep from the fold of a shepherd, Hannah. The day before Stephen''s trial, he was told that he was to stand in a lineup. Stephen asked for his lawyer to be present at the lineup but was told that he had no right to his lawyer''s presence. When he refused to take part, the officers said, "It will go hard for you if you refuse." Stephen then stood in the lineup. Five other men stood with him, all of approximately the same height, build, and complexion as Stephen. At Stephen''s trial, Hannah testified that she had been bringing her flock down from the hills at dusk on the night of the theft when she saw a man driving several of her sheep away. She said that she recognized Stephen as the man whom she had identified as the thief at a lineup the day before.

