    '16021_motorboat-sinker-stephen', 'CRIMINAL', 'Homicide', 'Manslaughter',
    'Stephen holds a state motorboat operator''s certificate and has done so for twelve years. While away caring for a sick relative, he let the certificate expire. When he returned home, he intended to renew it but never got around to it. Although a state statute made it a misdemeanor to operate a motorboat on public waterways without a valid operator''s certificate, Stephen continued to take his boat out regularly. One afternoon, while steering across a busy lake, he accidentally dropped a metal fishing sinker on the deck. He groped around the deck with one hand to find it while continuing to steer with the other. After locating the sinker, he glanced down from the water for a moment to pick it up and did not see Hannah, a kayaker who had just emerged from behind a moored boat. Stephen''s vessel struck Hannah, who died from her injuries. If Stephen is charged with homicide as a result of Hannah''s death, which of the following would be the prosecutor''s most effective argument?', 'Stephen holds a state motorboat operator''s certificate and has done so for twelve years. While away caring for a sick relative, he let the certificate expire. When he returned home, he intended to renew it but never got around to it. Although a state statute made it a misdemeanor to operate a motorboat on public waterways without a valid operator''s certificate, Stephen continued to take his boat out regularly. One afternoon, while steering across a busy lake, he accidentally dropped a metal fishing sinker on the deck. He groped around the deck with one hand to find it while continuing to steer with the other. After locating the sinker, he glanced down from the water for a moment to pick it up and did not see Hannah, a kayaker who had just emerged from behind a moored boat. Stephen''s vessel struck Hannah, who died from her injuries. If Stephen is charged with homicide as a result of Hannah''s death, which of the following would be the prosecutor''s most effective argument?', 'Which of 