    '16028_lydia_holy_cloth', 'CRIMINAL', 'Other Crimes', 'False pretenses',
    'Lydia worked as an antiques dealer who specialized in biblical artifacts. Timothy, a missionary preparing to travel to a remote region with a history of violent incidents, came to her shop seeking spiritual protection for his journey. Lydia offered to sell him a piece of woven cloth that she described as an authenticated fragment of the tabernacle used in biblical times, telling him it had been carbon-dated and certified by scholars and that possessing it would provide supernatural protection to the faithful. She charged him $800. Lydia knew that the cloth was a piece she had cut from a hotel curtain the previous week and that it had no special provenance whatsoever, but she believed that if Timothy had sufficient faith in the relic''s power, his confidence would lead him to act so cautiously and prayerfully on his mission that he would avoid any real danger. Timothy paid $800 for the cloth, carried it throughout his mission trip, and — believing he was under supernatural protection — ventured into a dangerous area he would otherwise have avoided. He was violently attacked there; although he survived, he suffered severe injuries and came close to death.', 'Lydia worked as an antiques dealer who specialized in biblical artifacts. Timothy, a missionary preparing to travel to a remote region with a history of violent incidents, came to her shop seeking spiritual protection for his journey. Lydia offered to sell him a piece of woven cloth that she described as an authenticated fragment of the tabernacle used in biblical times, telling him it had been carbon-dated and certified by scholars and that possessing it would provide supernatural protection to the faithful. She charged him $800. Lydia knew that the cloth was a piece she had cut from a hotel curtain the previous week and that it had no special provenance whatsoever, but she believed that if Timothy had sufficient faith in the relic''s power, his confidence would lead him to act so cautiously and prayerfully 