    'A state statute provides that "any person who brings about the death of another human being with the intent to cause said death or in the course of committing burglary, rape, robbery, or kidnapping shall be guilty of murder in the first degree." The jurisdiction applies common law definitions for the four enumerated felonies.

Barnabas planned to steal expensive outboard motors from locked storage cages at Harbor Cove Marina. He told his friend Stephen to wait in the getaway boat tied to the dock with its engine running around the corner. Barnabas used an angle grinder to cut through the padlock on the storage cage. The angle grinder''s sparks ignited spilled fuel pooled on the dock planks. The fire raced along the fuel sheen, reached the boat, and engulfed it. Stephen died from smoke inhalation before he could escape.', 'A state statute provides that "any person who brings about the death of another human being with the intent to cause said death or in the course of committing burglary, rape, robbery, or kidnapping shall be guilty of murder in the first degree." The jurisdiction applies common law definitions for the four enumerated felonies.

