    '16045_christian-tutor-bribery', 'CRIMINAL', 'General Principles', 'Parties to Crime — Accessories',
    'Peter wanted to hire a private bar-prep tutor. He learned that Lydia, the tutor-coordinator at Grace Prep Academy, was the person who decided which tutors got hired. Eager to get a spot, Peter offered Lydia his first month''s tutoring fee if she would hire her. Lydia accepted the offer and assigned Peter a tutor, and later accepted the payment from Peter. The state charged both Peter and Lydia under a statute that makes it a felony for "any person responsible for hiring tutors to solicit or demand anything of value from a hired tutor in exchange for the hiring." Lydia was charged as a principal and Peter as an accessory. They were tried jointly.

**A.** he did not assist Lydia in committing the crime.

**B.** a person cannot be tried as an accessory until the principal has first been tried and convicted.

**C.** the statute was intended to protect people in Peter''s position against people in Lydia''s position.

**D.** no person can be charged as an accessory to a crime that could not have been committed without his participation.', 'Peter wanted to hire a private bar-prep tutor. He learned that Lydia, the tutor-coordinator at Grace Prep Academy, was the person who decided which tutors got hired. Eager to get a spot, Peter offered Lydia his first month''s tutoring fee if she would hire her. Lydia accepted the offer and assigned Peter a tutor, and later accepted the payment from Peter. The state charged both Peter and Lydia under a statute that makes it a felony for "any person responsible for hiring tutors to solicit or demand anything of value from a hired tutor in exchange for the hiring." Lydia was charged as a principal and Peter as an accessory. They were tried jointly.

