    'Esther serves as director of a small Christian community center and wanted to obtain a parking variance allowing the center to use a municipal lot across the street for overflow parking during evening events. Fearing the city zoning board would deny the application, she spoke to a zoning office clerk named John. John told Esther that if she paid him $1,200, he would alter the variance application records to show the board had already approved it. Esther agreed and promised to bring the money the following morning. When she arrived at John''s office with the cash, she was told that John had resigned the previous day. A statute in the jurisdiction provides: "Any person who shall give or accept a fee not authorized by law as consideration for the act of any public employee is guilty of bribery, a felony. Any person who shall offer to commit a bribery is guilty of bribery in the second degree, a felony."', 'Esther serves as director of a small Christian community center and wanted to obtain a parking variance allowing the center to use a municipal lot across the street for overflow parking during evening events. Fearing the city zoning board would deny the application, she spoke to a zoning office clerk named John. John told Esther that if she paid him $1,200, he would alter the variance application records to show the board had already approved it. Esther agreed and promised to bring the money the following morning. When she arrived at John''s office with the cash, she was told that John had resigned the previous day. A statute in the jurisdiction provides: "Any person who shall give or accept a fee not authorized by law as consideration for the act of any public employee is guilty of bribery, a felony. Any person who shall offer to commit a bribery is guilty of bribery in the second degree, a felony."', 'Esther is prosecuted for attempted bribery in the second degree. The court should find her',
