    '16123_peter_gospel_trivia_getaway', 'CRIMINAL', 'Homicide', 'Manslaughter',
    'Peter put nearly all of his rent money into an informal cash pool tied to the final round of a televised gospel-trivia tournament. If his pick lost, he expected to lose his apartment. He watched the final round at a cafe that stayed open late for the event. During the close finish, Peter became so anxious that he drank several strong ciders and became drunk.

Peter''s pick won at the last moment. As Peter left the cafe, he saw two large men near the doorway who helped run the cash pool. Fearing that the men were angry about his win and were going to hurt him, Peter got into his car and drove away. A police officer saw Peter weaving across lanes and tried to pull him over. A reasonable sober driver would have recognized the car as a police car, but Peter thought the cash-pool helpers were chasing him.

Peter made a sudden turn onto a busy side street. Naomi was crossing the street while looking down at her phone and without looking up. Peter hit Naomi with the car, and Naomi died immediately. Peter was charged with involuntary manslaughter.', 'Peter put nearly all of his rent money into an informal cash pool tied to the final round of a televised gospel-trivia tournament. If his pick lost, he expected to lose his apartment. He watched the final round at a cafe that stayed open late for the event. During the close finish, Peter became so anxious that he drank several strong ciders and became drunk.

Peter''s pick won at the last moment. As Peter left the cafe, he saw two large men near the doorway who helped run the cash pool. Fearing that the men were angry about his win and were going to hurt him, Peter got into his car and drove away. A police officer saw Peter weaving across lanes and tried to pull him over. A reasonable sober driver would have recognized the car as a police car, but Peter thought the cash-pool helpers were chasing him.

Peter made a sudden turn onto a busy side street. Naomi was crossing the street while looking down at her phone and without looking up. Peter hit Naomi with the car, and Naomi died immediately. Peter was charged with involuntary manslaughter.', 'Peter should be found',
