Daniel is charged under a strict-liability agricultural-safety statute that makes it a misdemeanor to "apply uninspected pesticide on food-producing crops." Which of the following best describes the effect of Daniel''s reasonable, good-faith reliance on his supplier?', 'Daniel held a valid pesticide-application license issued by the state. A state regulation prohibited applying any pesticide on food-producing crops unless the pesticide batch had been inspected and certified by a state agricultural officer. For seven years Daniel had purchased pesticide concentrate from a single supplier who consistently delivered certified batches. Without Daniel''s knowledge, the supplier''s state certification had lapsed before the latest delivery, making that shipment uncertified. Daniel applied the pesticide to a field of leafy greens intended for retail sale. Several consumers who purchased and ate the greens became ill.

