**B.** Peter might face attempted murder charges for trying to kill John based on his act of cutting the rope.

**C.** Peter is not guilty of malicious destruction of property under transferred intent because the doctrine does not operate across different crime types.

**D.** Peter is not guilty of any crime because John was unharmed.', 'Which of the following correctly states the law?',
