    'After a late Christian apologetics night at a privately owned coffeehouse, Naomi carried a box of hymnals across the dark parking lot. Peter, a much larger man, brushed hard against her and knocked the box from her hands. He muttered, "Watch it — I ought to beat you senseless." Peter then turned toward the bus stop and walked away. Naomi believed he was only pretending to leave and was going to circle behind the parked vans to attack her. She took a pocketknife from her coat, ran up behind Peter, and stabbed him in the back, killing him. Several bystanders later said Peter continued toward the bus stop and made no move to turn back. Naomi testifies that she was genuinely terrified and certain Peter would attack. If Naomi is charged with murder, what is the most likely outcome?', 'After a late Christian apologetics night at a privately owned coffeehouse, Naomi carried a box of hymnals across the dark parking lot. Peter, a much larger man, brushed hard against her and knocked the box from her hands. He muttered, "Watch it — I ought to beat you senseless." Peter then turned toward the bus stop and walked away. Naomi believed he was only pretending to leave and was going to circle behind the parked vans to attack her. She took a pocketknife from her coat, ran up behind Peter, and stabbed him in the back, killing him. Several bystanders later said Peter continued toward the bus stop and made no move to turn back. Naomi testifies that she was genuinely terrified and certain Peter would attack. If Naomi is charged with murder, what is the most likely outcome?', 'If Naomi is charged with murder, what is the most likely outcome?',
