    'Timothy was arrested outside a county harvest-jubilee fairground and taken to the sheriff''s annex. A deputy gave Timothy his Miranda warnings, and Timothy said that he wanted to speak with a lawyer before talking to anyone. Just then, the deputy was called away to help restrain an intoxicated man who had started shouting in the booking area. About an hour later, another deputy opened the holding-room door and asked, "Do you need water or a blanket?" Timothy replied, "Yeah, a good lawyer, because everybody knows I torched Barnabas''s food trailer." At trial, Timothy moves to exclude that statement. How should the court rule?', 'Timothy was arrested outside a county harvest-jubilee fairground and taken to the sheriff''s annex. A deputy gave Timothy his Miranda warnings, and Timothy said that he wanted to speak with a lawyer before talking to anyone. Just then, the deputy was called away to help restrain an intoxicated man who had started shouting in the booking area. About an hour later, another deputy opened the holding-room door and asked, "Do you need water or a blanket?" Timothy replied, "Yeah, a good lawyer, because everybody knows I torched Barnabas''s food trailer." At trial, Timothy moves to exclude that statement. How should the court rule?', 'How should the court rule?',
