    'A palm-sized silver-and-garnet Scripture case used to hold handwritten prayer cards disappeared from Lydia''s table during a riverfront gospel fair. Officers on bicycle patrol were radioed to watch for whoever had taken it. Minutes later, an officer saw Daniel cutting across a nearby soccer field away from the fair tents, breathing hard. The officer stopped Daniel and asked his name and why he was leaving so quickly. Daniel replied, "Just trying to catch my ride." The officer then ordered Daniel to raise his hands and patted the outside of his jacket to see whether he had the missing Scripture case. She felt a hard object in one pocket and, thinking it was the case, reached inside. The object was a pistol, and Daniel lacked the permit required by law to carry it concealed. Before Daniel''s trial for unlawful possession of a concealed weapon, he moved to suppress the pistol. Should the motion be granted?', 'A palm-sized silver-and-garnet Scripture case used to hold handwritten prayer cards disappeared from Lydia''s table during a riverfront gospel fair. Officers on bicycle patrol were radioed to watch for whoever had taken it. Minutes later, an officer saw Daniel cutting across a nearby soccer field away from the fair tents, breathing hard. The officer stopped Daniel and asked his name and why he was leaving so quickly. Daniel replied, "Just trying to catch my ride." The officer then ordered Daniel to raise his hands and patted the outside of his jacket to see whether he had the missing Scripture case. She felt a hard object in one pocket and, thinking it was the case, reached inside. The object was a pistol, and Daniel lacked the permit required by law to carry it concealed. Before Daniel''s trial for unlawful possession of a concealed weapon, he moved to suppress the pistol. Should the motion be granted?', 'Should the motion to suppress the pistol be granted?',
