Martha later called Hannah, her own expert, and asked, “Do you accept Lydia’s handbook as reliable?” Hannah answered, “It once was, but it is now badly out of date.” Peter requested that the jury be allowed to examine the handbook and judge for itself the handbook’s reliability.', 'At a federal civil trial for professional malpractice, Peter claimed that Martha, an electrical engineer, had negligently specified undersized motors for the rotating Bethlehem-star display at Peter’s private Nativity-themed mini-golf course.

