    '14824_banner_drone', 'EVIDENCE', 'Presentation of Evidence', 'Preliminary questions',
    'At a private Christian makers'' fair, Hannah was struck by a banner drone carrying hand-lettered Psalms after Timothy, the drone operator, launched it toward the exhibit hall. Hannah later died from the injury. Lydia, Hannah''s executor, sued Timothy for wrongful death. At trial, Lydia calls Ruth, a nurse, to testify that the next morning, Hannah said to Ruth, ''Timothy launched the banner drone after the marshal dropped the landing flag.'' Twelve minutes later, Hannah died. To lay the foundation for Hannah''s statement, Lydia offers the court an affidavit from Dr. Luke stating that he was the attending physician that morning and that Hannah had said several times that she knew she was about to die.', 'At a private Christian makers'' fair, Hannah was struck by a banner drone carrying hand-lettered Psalms after Timothy, the drone operator, launched it toward the exhibit hall. Hannah later died from the injury. Lydia, Hannah''s executor, sued Timothy for wrongful death. At trial, Lydia calls Ruth, a nurse, to testify that the next morning, Hannah said to Ruth, ''Timothy launched the banner drone after the marshal dropped the landing flag.'' Twelve minutes later, Hannah died. To lay the foundation for Hannah''s statement, Lydia offers the court an affidavit from Dr. Luke stating that he was the attending physician that morning and that Hannah had said several times that she knew she was about to die.', 'Is the affidavit properly considered by the court in ruling on the admissibility of Hannah''s statement?',
