) VALUES (
    '14825_pantry-volunteer-incident-report', 'EVIDENCE', 'Presentation of Evidence', 'Refreshing recollection',
    'Lydia has volunteered for years at Grace Community Food Pantry, a Christian ministry that gives groceries to families in need. She was working the distribution line on a busy Saturday when a man she later identified as the defendant took several boxes of donated canned goods from the loading area without authorization and loaded them into his truck. At trial for theft, Lydia testified for the prosecution. Before she took the stand, she had trouble remembering the exact sequence of what she saw the defendant load and carry. To prepare, she refreshed her memory by silently reviewing a short incident report that Timothy, the pantry''s volunteer coordinator, had written the day after the event.

**A:** The court must allow the examination, but only to the extent that the report contains Lydia''s own statement to Timothy.

**B:** The court should not allow the examination, because the report was not shown to have been read and approved by Lydia while the matter was fresh in her mind.

**C:** The court may allow the examination if the report was used by Lydia to refresh her memory before testifying, and must allow it if she used it during her testimony.

**D:** The court should not allow the examination, unless the report was used by Lydia to refresh her memory while on the witness stand.', 'Lydia has volunteered for years at Grace Community Food Pantry, a Christian ministry that gives groceries to families in need. She was working the distribution line on a busy Saturday when a man she later identified as the defendant took several boxes of donated canned goods from the loading area without authorization and loaded them into his truck. At trial for theft, Lydia testified for the prosecution. Before she took the stand, she had trouble remembering the exact sequence of what she saw the defendant load and carry. To prepare, she refreshed her memory by silently reviewing a short incident report that Timothy, the pantry''s volunteer coordinator, had written the day after the event.

