    'Peter is the defendant in a civil suit brought by Paul, a former deckhand who was injured when Peter''s forty-foot charter boat struck a channel marker in rough weather. During pretrial discovery, Paul listed Lydia, who had been the bookkeeper at Peter''s marina office, as a witness to certain fuel-log and maintenance irregularities.

