    'After a written demand letter claimed $18,000 in damages from a ruined wedding photo album, the photography studio disputed both liability and amount. During a settlement meeting, the studio''s partner said, "We were probably 75 percent at fault for not backing up the memory card, so we will write a check for $4,500." The plaintiff offers the statement at trial to prove the studio''s liability. How should the court rule?

