    difficulty, status, source_type, version, metadata
) VALUES (
    '19251_state_park_detention', 'EVIDENCE', 'Privileges and Public Policy Exclusions', 'Physician-patient',
    'A youth group from Grace Community Church is on a weekend retreat at Cedar Hollow State Park. While the group is hiking a marked trail, a state park ranger stops them and claims they lack a required trail permit. When the youth pastor, **Stephen**, tries to calmly explain the group''s reservation, the ranger shoves him to the ground, fracturing his wrist. Stephen is taken to a local urgent-care clinic and treated by **Dr. Lois**, who records Stephen''s account of the encounter. Stephen sues the ranger in federal court under a federal civil-rights statute, alleging excessive force. The state where the park is located has a physician-patient privilege statute. Stephen moves to exclude Dr. Lois''s testimony by invoking that state statute. Which ruling is most proper on Stephen''s privilege objection?', 'A youth group from Grace Community Church is on a weekend retreat at Cedar Hollow State Park. While the group is hiking a marked trail, a state park ranger stops them and claims they lack a required trail permit. When the youth pastor, **Stephen**, tries to calmly explain the group''s reservation, the ranger shoves him to the ground, fracturing his wrist. Stephen is taken to a local urgent-care clinic and treated by **Dr. Lois**, who records Stephen''s account of the encounter. Stephen sues the ranger in federal court under a federal civil-rights statute, alleging excessive force. The state where the park is located has a physician-patient privilege statute. Stephen moves to exclude Dr. Lois''s testimony by invoking that state statute. Which ruling is most proper on Stephen''s privilege objection?', 'Which ruling is most proper on Stephen''s privilege objection?',
