    'Executing a valid warrant, police raided a rented civic auditorium during a Holy Week outreach event, lawfully arresting Stephen, the director of a small Christian theater troupe, and lawfully seizing a video recording of the Passion Play performance that he had staged. Stephen was subsequently charged with “conducting an obscene dramatic performance” in violation of a state law. At trial, the prosecution called a professor to the stand. The professor testified that she was a professor of theater arts and the author of several books on the art of biblical drama. She said that although she believed biblical drama to be a valid art form, she found the performance at issue to be devoid of any literary or artistic merit. She stated further that in her opinion it was obscene. In objecting to this testimony, which of the following would be Stephen''s most effective argument?', 'Executing a valid warrant, police raided a rented civic auditorium during a Holy Week outreach event, lawfully arresting Stephen, the director of a small Christian theater troupe, and lawfully seizing a video recording of the Passion Play performance that he had staged. Stephen was subsequently charged with “conducting an obscene dramatic performance” in violation of a state law. At trial, the prosecution called a professor to the stand. The professor testified that she was a professor of theater arts and the author of several books on the art of biblical drama. She said that although she believed biblical drama to be a valid art form, she found the performance at issue to be devoid of any literary or artistic merit. She stated further that in her opinion it was obscene. In objecting to this testimony, which of the following would be Stephen''s most effective argument?', 'In objecting to this testimony, which of the following would be Stephen''s most effective argument?',
