    '22164_tractor', 'EVIDENCE', 'Presentation of Evidence', 'General Provisions',
    'A state statute requires every person who operates a farm tractor on public roads to carry a policy of agricultural liability insurance with a minimum coverage of $25,000. Violation is a misdemeanor. After a collision on a county road between a tractor operated by David and a horse-drawn cart driven by Ruth, David was cited and convicted of operating an uninsured tractor in violation of the statute. David later died, and Ruth brought a negligence action against David''s estate for her injuries. During jury selection, Ruth''s attorney asked each prospective juror whether he or she held any shares in any agricultural liability insurance company. At trial, David''s estate''s attorney offered into evidence the judgment of David''s conviction for operating an uninsured tractor. Ruth''s attorney objected. Should the judgment be admitted?', 'A state statute requires every person who operates a farm tractor on public roads to carry a policy of agricultural liability insurance with a minimum coverage of $25,000. Violation is a misdemeanor. After a collision on a county road between a tractor operated by David and a horse-drawn cart driven by Ruth, David was cited and convicted of operating an uninsured tractor in violation of the statute. David later died, and Ruth brought a negligence action against David''s estate for her injuries. During jury selection, Ruth''s attorney asked each prospective juror whether he or she held any shares in any agricultural liability insurance company. At trial, David''s estate''s attorney offered into evidence the judgment of David''s conviction for operating an uninsured tractor. Ruth''s attorney objected. Should the judgment be admitted?', 'Should the judgment be admitted?',
