    '22210_gospel_tour_van', 'EVIDENCE', 'Presentation of Evidence', 'Prior inconsistent statement',
    'After a late-night gospel concert, sheriff''s deputies stopped a van being driven by Daniel and forced him to open the rear cargo compartment. Inside they found a canvas duffel containing several pounds of methamphetamine. They seized the van and the drugs and placed Daniel under arrest. Without advising him of his rights to remain silent and to consult with an attorney, they questioned him about the drugs. During the questioning, Daniel said, "I do not know anything about them. It is not even my van." Daniel was charged with unlawful possession of a controlled substance. Later, Daniel''s motion to suppress the methamphetamine was granted, and the charges were dismissed. Daniel then brought an appropriate civil action against the sheriff''s department to recover the seized van. During his direct case, Daniel testified that he owned the van but had registered it in Timothy''s name for convenience. On cross-examination, the department''s lawyer asked, "After your arrest, did you tell the deputies that it was not your van?" If Daniel''s lawyer objects to this question, should the objection be sustained?', 'After a late-night gospel concert, sheriff''s deputies stopped a van being driven by Daniel and forced him to open the rear cargo compartment. Inside they found a canvas duffel containing several pounds of methamphetamine. They seized the van and the drugs and placed Daniel under arrest. Without advising him of his rights to remain silent and to consult with an attorney, they questioned him about the drugs. During the questioning, Daniel said, "I do not know anything about them. It is not even my van." Daniel was charged with unlawful possession of a controlled substance. Later, Daniel''s motion to suppress the methamphetamine was granted, and the charges were dismissed. Daniel then brought an appropriate civil action against the sheriff''s department to recover the seized van. During his direct case, Daniel testified that he owned the van but had registered it 