) VALUES (
    '22229_stephen-canoe', 'EVIDENCE', 'Privileges and Other Policy Exclusions', 'Liability insurance',
    'Stephen invited Barnabas to go canoeing on a river near their town. While navigating a stretch of rapids, Stephen lost control of the canoe and it struck a submerged rock. Barnabas was thrown from the canoe and struck his head on a boulder. He was hospitalized for six weeks with a serious head injury. Barnabas subsequently filed a negligence action against Stephen. At trial, on direct examination, Barnabas testified that immediately after the accident, while Stephen was visibly shaken and upset, Stephen said, "Don''t worry, my watercraft policy has plenty of coverage." Upon objection by Stephen''s attorney, should that portion of Barnabas''s testimony be excluded?

**A)** No, because it is an excited utterance.
**B)** Yes, because it is not relevant to a material issue.
**C)** No, because it is an admission of a party.
**D)** Yes, because it relates to a compromise offer.', 'Stephen invited Barnabas to go canoeing on a river near their town. While navigating a stretch of rapids, Stephen lost control of the canoe and it struck a submerged rock. Barnabas was thrown from the canoe and struck his head on a boulder. He was hospitalized for six weeks with a serious head injury. Barnabas subsequently filed a negligence action against Stephen. At trial, on direct examination, Barnabas testified that immediately after the accident, while Stephen was visibly shaken and upset, Stephen said, "Don''t worry, my watercraft policy has plenty of coverage." Upon objection by Stephen''s attorney, should that portion of Barnabas''s testimony be excluded?

