    '14988_missionary_acreage', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Ownership', 'Joint tenancy',
    'A retired missionary and widower named Barnabas conveyed the riverside homestead acreage by quitclaim deed to his daughter Lydia and his son Silas “as joint tenants in fee simple.” The language of the deed was sufficient to create a common law joint tenancy with right of survivorship, which is unmodified by statute. Lydia then duly executed a will devising her interest in the acreage to her close friend and prayer partner Priscilla. Silas then duly executed a will devising his interest in the acreage to his cousin Timothy. Silas died, and later Lydia died. Neither had ever married. Priscilla and Timothy survived. After both wills have been duly probated, who owns what interest in the acreage?', 'A retired missionary and widower named Barnabas conveyed the riverside homestead acreage by quitclaim deed to his daughter Lydia and his son Silas “as joint tenants in fee simple.” The language of the deed was sufficient to create a common law joint tenancy with right of survivorship, which is unmodified by statute. Lydia then duly executed a will devising her interest in the acreage to her close friend and prayer partner Priscilla. Silas then duly executed a will devising his interest in the acreage to his cousin Timothy. Silas died, and later Lydia died. Neither had ever married. Priscilla and Timothy survived. After both wills have been duly probated, who owns what interest in the acreage?', 'After both wills have been duly probated, who owns what interest in the acreage?',
