    '14994_cedaracre_scripture_orchard', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Ownership', 'Contingent and vested remainders',
    'Naomi owned Cedaracre, a wooded parcel where her family held private Scripture-copying weekends, in fee simple. Naomi wrote and executed, with all required formalities, a will that devised Cedaracre to "my daughter Mary for life, with remainder to my descendants per stirpes." When Naomi signed the will, she had a husband, Daniel, and no living descendants other than her two children, Mary and Paul. Naomi later died, and the will was duly admitted to probate. Daniel had predeceased her. Naomi was survived by Mary, Paul, three grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren. Mary and Paul were Naomi''s sole heirs at law. Mary and Paul brought an appropriate declaratory-judgment action to determine title to Cedaracre. Guardians ad litem were appointed, and all other steps were taken so that the judgment would bind all interested persons, born or unborn. In that action, if the court rules that Mary has a life estate in all of Cedaracre and that the remainder is contingent, it will be because the court chose one of several possible constructions and that construction', 'Naomi owned Cedaracre, a wooded parcel where her family held private Scripture-copying weekends, in fee simple. Naomi wrote and executed, with all required formalities, a will that devised Cedaracre to "my daughter Mary for life, with remainder to my descendants per stirpes." When Naomi signed the will, she had a husband, Daniel, and no living descendants other than her two children, Mary and Paul. Naomi later died, and the will was duly admitted to probate. Daniel had predeceased her. Naomi was survived by Mary, Paul, three grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren. Mary and Paul were Naomi''s sole heirs at law. Mary and Paul brought an appropriate declaratory-judgment action to determine title to Cedaracre. Guardians ad litem were appointed, and all other steps were taken so that the judgment would bind all interested persons, born or unborn. In that action, if the court rules that Mary has a life esta