    '15011_psalm_ridge_meadow', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Rights in Land', 'Easements',
    'Daniel owned a private mountain tract called Psalm Ridge. The front portion touched a county road, and the tract had no access to any other road. Eighteen years ago, Daniel conveyed the rear meadow to Ruth and at the same time granted Ruth an express driveway easement across Daniel''s retained front land to the county road. Ruth used the driveway until she conveyed the meadow back to Daniel 11 years ago. The deed back to Daniel did not mention the easement. Six years ago, Daniel again conveyed the rear meadow, this time to Lydia, by a deed that did not mention any easement to the county road. Recently, Daniel told Lydia that she could no longer cross Daniel''s front land to reach the county road. Naomi, a neighbor, told Lydia that Lydia could cross Naomi''s land to reach a different county road if Lydia paid for that right. Lydia has sued Daniel for the right to cross Daniel''s land to the county road. For whom will the court likely decide?', 'Daniel owned a private mountain tract called Psalm Ridge. The front portion touched a county road, and the tract had no access to any other road. Eighteen years ago, Daniel conveyed the rear meadow to Ruth and at the same time granted Ruth an express driveway easement across Daniel''s retained front land to the county road. Ruth used the driveway until she conveyed the meadow back to Daniel 11 years ago. The deed back to Daniel did not mention the easement. Six years ago, Daniel again conveyed the rear meadow, this time to Lydia, by a deed that did not mention any easement to the county road. Recently, Daniel told Lydia that she could no longer cross Daniel''s front land to reach the county road. Naomi, a neighbor, told Lydia that Lydia could cross Naomi''s land to reach a different county road if Lydia paid for that right. Lydia has sued Daniel for the right to cross Daniel''s land to the county road. For whom will the court likely decide?', 'For whom will the court likely decide?',
