    difficulty, status, source_type, version, metadata
) VALUES (
    '15022_psalm_lane_covenant', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Rights in Land', 'Equitable Servitudes / Restrictive Covenants',
    'Naomi owned five adjoining cottage parcels, labeled A through E, all fronting on Psalm Lane. The parcels were in a zoning district that allowed one- and two-family residences. Two years ago, Naomi conveyed Parcels A, C, and E. None of those three deeds contained any use restriction. Each buyer built a one-family cottage.

One year ago, Naomi conveyed Parcel B to Lydia. The deed provided that Lydia and Naomi, and their respective heirs and assigns, would use Parcels B and D, respectively, only for one-family residential purposes. The deed was promptly and properly recorded. Lydia built a one-family cottage on Parcel B.

Last month, Naomi conveyed Parcel D to Timothy. The deed to Timothy contained no use restriction. The recorded deed from Naomi to Lydia appeared in the title report that Timothy''s lawyer examined. Timothy obtained a building permit and began construction of a two-family residence on Parcel D.

Lydia, joined by the owners of Parcels A, C, and E, brought an appropriate action against Timothy to enjoin the proposed use of Parcel D or, alternatively, to recover damages caused by Timothy''s breach of covenant.', 'Naomi owned five adjoining cottage parcels, labeled A through E, all fronting on Psalm Lane. The parcels were in a zoning district that allowed one- and two-family residences. Two years ago, Naomi conveyed Parcels A, C, and E. None of those three deeds contained any use restriction. Each buyer built a one-family cottage.

One year ago, Naomi conveyed Parcel B to Lydia. The deed provided that Lydia and Naomi, and their respective heirs and assigns, would use Parcels B and D, respectively, only for one-family residential purposes. The deed was promptly and properly recorded. Lydia built a one-family cottage on Parcel B.

Last month, Naomi conveyed Parcel D to Timothy. The deed to Timothy contained no use restriction. The recorded deed from Naomi to Lydia appeared in the title report that Timothy''s lawyer examined. Timothy obtained a building permit and began construction of a two-family residence on Parcel D.

Lydia, joined by the owners of Parcels A, C, and E, brought an appropriate action against Timothy to enjoin the proposed use of Parcel D or, alternatively, to recover damages caused by Timothy''s breach of covenant.', 'Which is the most appropriate comment concerning the outcome of this action?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "15022", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "81020502", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
