    '15035_damascus_alley', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Rights in Land', 'Easements — termination/remedies for misuse',
    'Barnabas owns Damascus Yard, a converted riverfront warehouse parcel used for a small Christian bookbinding studio and apartment. The parcel is boxed in by other lots, and its only access to a public street is a deeded easement over Lydia’s 18-foot loading alley. Lydia owns the neighboring parcel. Barnabas paved the alley route, and for 14 years the alley was used without incident. Last spring, as permitted by the zoning ordinance, Barnabas built a 140-seat Bible-map escape room and coffee courtyard on Damascus Yard, using all available space on the parcel. The attraction became popular. On Saturday evenings, visitors overflowed the courtyard’s parking area and parked along the loading alley for hours. After three Saturdays of congestion, Lydia stretched a chain across the alley on Saturday evenings to block anyone seeking access to Damascus Yard. Barnabas objected. Lydia brought an appropriate action to terminate the easement.', 'Barnabas owns Damascus Yard, a converted riverfront warehouse parcel used for a small Christian bookbinding studio and apartment. The parcel is boxed in by other lots, and its only access to a public street is a deeded easement over Lydia’s 18-foot loading alley. Lydia owns the neighboring parcel. Barnabas paved the alley route, and for 14 years the alley was used without incident. Last spring, as permitted by the zoning ordinance, Barnabas built a 140-seat Bible-map escape room and coffee courtyard on Damascus Yard, using all available space on the parcel. The attraction became popular. On Saturday evenings, visitors overflowed the courtyard’s parking area and parked along the loading alley for hours. After three Saturdays of congestion, Lydia stretched a chain across the alley on Saturday evenings to block anyone seeking access to Damascus Yard. Barnabas objected. Lydia brought an appropriate action to terminate the easement.', 'The most likely result in this action is that the court will hold for:',
