    '15041_scripture_print_studio_lien', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Titles', 'Titles, Deeds, and Conveyancing',
    'Twelve years ago, Martha bought a brick studio lot for a Scripture-printing shop from a seller. Martha financed the purchase price with a loan from Cedar Bank that was secured by a mortgage on the lot. At closing, Martha bought a title insurance policy naming both Martha and Cedar Bank, and the policy showed no liens on the lot except Cedar Bank''s mortgage. Nine years ago, Martha paid the Cedar Bank loan in full. Five years ago, Martha sold the studio lot to Timothy by a general warranty deed with no exceptions. Three years ago, Timothy transferred the studio lot to Lydia by a quitclaim deed as a gift. This spring, Lydia discovered an old mortgage on the lot that predated all of these transfers. Because a title examiner negligently missed the old mortgage, it had not been disclosed in the title insurance policy issued to Martha and Cedar Bank. Lydia successfully sued Martha on Martha''s warranty deed and recovered the amount of the old mortgage. If Martha sues the title insurance company to recover the amount she paid Lydia, is Martha likely to prevail?', 'Twelve years ago, Martha bought a brick studio lot for a Scripture-printing shop from a seller. Martha financed the purchase price with a loan from Cedar Bank that was secured by a mortgage on the lot. At closing, Martha bought a title insurance policy naming both Martha and Cedar Bank, and the policy showed no liens on the lot except Cedar Bank''s mortgage. Nine years ago, Martha paid the Cedar Bank loan in full. Five years ago, Martha sold the studio lot to Timothy by a general warranty deed with no exceptions. Three years ago, Timothy transferred the studio lot to Lydia by a quitclaim deed as a gift. This spring, Lydia discovered an old mortgage on the lot that predated all of these transfers. Because a title examiner negligently missed the old mortgage, it had not been disclosed in the title insurance policy issued to Martha and Cedar Bank. Lydia successfully sued Martha on Martha''s warranty deed and recovered the amount of the old mortgage. If Martha sues the title insurance company to recover the amount she paid Lydia, is Martha likely to prevail?', 'If Martha sues the title insurance company to recover the amount she paid Lydia, is Martha likely to prevail?',
