) VALUES (
    '15074_forged-deed-church-parcel', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Titles', 'Forged instruments',
    'Barnabas owned five adjacent parcels of farmland. He borrowed $40,000 from a credit union and gave the credit union a promissory note and a deed of trust encumbering all five parcels. The deed of trust was promptly and properly recorded. After Barnabas repaid $8,000, the credit union executed and delivered to him a valid release of Parcel 3. Barnabas altered the release document to also include Parcel 5, then recorded the altered instrument. He thereafter sold Parcel 5 to Lydia, an innocent purchaser for value. When the credit union discovered the alteration, it brought an appropriate action against Barnabas and Lydia to set aside the release as to Parcel 5. Barnabas did not defend, but Lydia did. The jurisdiction''s recording act provides: ''No unrecorded conveyance or mortgage of real property shall be good against subsequent purchasers for value without notice, who shall first record.''', 'Barnabas owned five adjacent parcels of farmland. He borrowed $40,000 from a credit union and gave the credit union a promissory note and a deed of trust encumbering all five parcels. The deed of trust was promptly and properly recorded. After Barnabas repaid $8,000, the credit union executed and delivered to him a valid release of Parcel 3. Barnabas altered the release document to also include Parcel 5, then recorded the altered instrument. He thereafter sold Parcel 5 to Lydia, an innocent purchaser for value. When the credit union discovered the alteration, it brought an appropriate action against Barnabas and Lydia to set aside the release as to Parcel 5. Barnabas did not defend, but Lydia did. The jurisdiction''s recording act provides: ''No unrecorded conveyance or mortgage of real property shall be good against subsequent purchasers for value without notice, who shall first record.''', 'The court should rule for',
