    'For 24 years, the land records have listed Daniel as owner of a vacant seven-acre greenhouse lot behind an old train depot. Daniel has never physically occupied the lot. Seventeen years ago, Esther entered the lot and turned it into a private Scripture-garden business, repairing the glass house, fencing the beds, tending fig trees, and excluding others. The character and duration of Esther''s possession of the lot caused her to become the owner of the lot under the adverse possession law of the jurisdiction.

