    'Six years ago, Lydia owned a hillside parcel called Psalm Grove. She conveyed Psalm Grove to Barnabas, but Barnabas did not record the deed he received from Lydia. Barnabas then sold Psalm Grove to Ruth, and Ruth promptly recorded the deed she received from Barnabas. Three years later, Ruth sold Psalm Grove to Timothy, who promptly recorded his deed. Two years after Timothy bought Psalm Grove, Lydia purported to sell Psalm Grove again to Esther, who immediately recorded her deed. The jurisdiction has a statute providing that no conveyance of real estate is effective against a subsequent purchaser for value without notice unless it has been recorded. The official recording office does not maintain a tract index. If Esther asserts that her title is superior to Timothy''s and sues Timothy to quiet title to Psalm Grove, which of the following would be Esther''s most effective argument?', 'Six years ago, Lydia owned a hillside parcel called Psalm Grove. She conveyed Psalm Grove to Barnabas, but Barnabas did not record the deed he received from Lydia. Barnabas then sold Psalm Grove to Ruth, and Ruth promptly recorded the deed she received from Barnabas. Three years later, Ruth sold Psalm Grove to Timothy, who promptly recorded his deed. Two years after Timothy bought Psalm Grove, Lydia purported to sell Psalm Grove again to Esther, who immediately recorded her deed. The jurisdiction has a statute providing that no conveyance of real estate is effective against a subsequent purchaser for value without notice unless it has been recorded. The official recording office does not maintain a tract index. If Esther asserts that her title is superior to Timothy''s and sues Timothy to quiet title to Psalm Grove, which of the following would be Esther''s most effective argument?', 'If Esther asserts that her title is superior to Timothy''s and sues Timothy to quiet title to Psalm Grove, which of the following would be Esther''s most effective argument?',
