For a year, Ruth made the payments on the note to Covenant Bank. Then a highway reroute sharply reduced foot traffic near the building, the property value dropped, and Ruth stopped making payments. Daniel''s mortgage contained a clause expressly permitting later buyers to take the premises "subject to the mortgage" and/or to "assume the mortgage."', 'When Daniel bought a small olive-press building and upstairs apartment near a Christian retreat district, he borrowed part of the purchase price from Covenant Bank. At the same closing where Daniel received title, he signed a promissory note payable to Covenant Bank and secured it with a mortgage on the building.

