For a year, Ruth made the payments on the note to Covenant Bank. Then a highway reroute sharply reduced foot traffic near the building, the property value dropped, and Ruth stopped making payments. Daniel''s mortgage contained a clause expressly permitting later buyers to take the premises "subject to the mortgage" and/or to "assume the mortgage."', 'If Covenant Bank sues Daniel, Lydia, and Barnabas on the note, from which of them is Covenant Bank entitled to recover?',
