    'Naomi, an ailing widow, executed a deed to her hillside vineyard naming her two sons, Daniel and Timothy, as joint tenants with full right of survivorship. Because Daniel was away on a long journey across the sea, Naomi handed the deed to Timothy, telling him to let Daniel know about it as soon as he returned. She explained that she was conveying the vineyard now, while she was alive, so that her sons would not be burdened with the inheritance levy, but that she wished to keep tending the vines and living in the farmhouse until her death. Timothy had the deed duly recorded at the land registry and then returned it to Naomi, asking her to keep it for him in her strongbox. Naomi went on tending the vineyard and living in the farmhouse for about six weeks, until she died. Timothy died ten days later, never having worked the vineyard and never having told Daniel about the conveyance. Naomi''s will left all her property to her sister, Lydia. Timothy''s will left all his property to his friend, Philemon.', 'Naomi, an ailing widow, executed a deed to her hillside vineyard naming her two sons, Daniel and Timothy, as joint tenants with full right of survivorship. Because Daniel was away on a long journey across the sea, Naomi handed the deed to Timothy, telling him to let Daniel know about it as soon as he returned. She explained that she was conveying the vineyard now, while she was alive, so that her sons would not be burdened with the inheritance levy, but that she wished to keep tending the vines and living in the farmhouse until her death. Timothy had the deed duly recorded at the land registry and then returned it to Naomi, asking her to keep it for him in her strongbox. Naomi went on tending the vineyard and living in the farmhouse for about six weeks, until she died. Timothy died ten days later, never having worked the vineyard and never having told Daniel about the conveyance. Naomi''s will left all her property to her sister, Lydia. Timothy''s will left all his property to his friend, Philemon.', 'Who is entitled to the vineyard?',
