) VALUES (
    '22017_silas_fig_orchard_escrow_delivery', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Titles', 'Delivery and acceptance',
    'On March 2, Martha and Silas signed a written contract for the sale of Martha''s riverside fig orchard parcel. When the contract was signed, Silas handed Martha a bank draft drawn on an out-of-region bank for the entire purchase price. As the contract directed, Martha executed a deed to the parcel and deposited it with a licensed escrow firm, instructing the firm to deliver the deed to Silas as soon as the draft cleared the bank.

The draft cleared the bank on March 14. Because a flood had closed the bank''s offices, the escrow firm did not learn that the draft had cleared until March 20 and did not deliver the deed to Silas until March 21. On March 16, Silas executed a deed purporting to convey the parcel to Philip.

A statute in the state makes it a misdemeanor for any person "to execute any document purporting to convey an interest in real estate that the person executing the document did not actually hold at the time the document was executed, whether or not that person knew he or she did not hold the interest the document purported to convey." If Silas is charged with violating this statute by executing the deed to Philip on March 16, should he be convicted?', 'On March 2, Martha and Silas signed a written contract for the sale of Martha''s riverside fig orchard parcel. When the contract was signed, Silas handed Martha a bank draft drawn on an out-of-region bank for the entire purchase price. As the contract directed, Martha executed a deed to the parcel and deposited it with a licensed escrow firm, instructing the firm to deliver the deed to Silas as soon as the draft cleared the bank.

The draft cleared the bank on March 14. Because a flood had closed the bank''s offices, the escrow firm did not learn that the draft had cleared until March 20 and did not deliver the deed to Silas until March 21. On March 16, Silas executed a deed purporting to convey the parcel to Philip.

A statute in the state makes it a misdemeanor for any person "to execute any document purporting to convey an interest in real estate that the person executing the document did not actually hold at the time the document was executed, whether or not that person knew he or she did not hold the interest the document purported to convey." If Silas is charged with violating this statute by executing the deed to Philip on March 16, should he be convicted?', 'If Silas is charged with violating this statute by executing the deed to Philip on March 16, should he be convicted?',
