    'Naomi owned a small lakeside cottage that she leased to Timothy under a four-year lease providing, "Tenant agrees that he or she will not assign or sublet the premises without the written permission of the landlord." Nine months after taking possession under the lease, Timothy — who was about to spend four months helping rebuild a meeting hall in a distant town — asked Naomi''s permission to sublet the cottage for that four-month period. Although Timothy offered to submit the names of prospective subtenants to Naomi for her approval, Naomi said that she would not approve a sublease to any person under any circumstances. Timothy thereafter sublet the premises to a sublessee.', 'Naomi owned a small lakeside cottage that she leased to Timothy under a four-year lease providing, "Tenant agrees that he or she will not assign or sublet the premises without the written permission of the landlord." Nine months after taking possession under the lease, Timothy — who was about to spend four months helping rebuild a meeting hall in a distant town — asked Naomi''s permission to sublet the cottage for that four-month period. Although Timothy offered to submit the names of prospective subtenants to Naomi for her approval, Naomi said that she would not approve a sublease to any person under any circumstances. Timothy thereafter sublet the premises to a sublessee.', 'Which of the following statements is most correct regarding the rights of Naomi?',
