    'Esther runs a small Christmas tree farm on a tight lot. After most holiday seasons — but not every year — she loads her truck with unsold tree stumps and trimming debris and hauls them to a remote clearing on her neighbor Daniel''s 15-acre rural property. Her own lot has no room for the waste. Daniel has never given Esther permission to do this, but he has always been aware of it. Esther has done this for most of the 35 holiday seasons she has operated her farm. Daniel recently sold the property to his son John. When Esther arrived with a truckload of stumps this past season, John told her she could no longer use the clearing. The state has a 20-year adverse possession statute.', 'Esther runs a small Christmas tree farm on a tight lot. After most holiday seasons — but not every year — she loads her truck with unsold tree stumps and trimming debris and hauls them to a remote clearing on her neighbor Daniel''s 15-acre rural property. Her own lot has no room for the waste. Daniel has never given Esther permission to do this, but he has always been aware of it. Esther has done this for most of the 35 holiday seasons she has operated her farm. Daniel recently sold the property to his son John. When Esther arrived with a truckload of stumps this past season, John told her she could no longer use the clearing. The state has a 20-year adverse possession statute.', 'Is Esther entitled to continue using the clearing to dump her tree waste?',
