) VALUES (
    '22062_private_bookshop_omitted_mortgagee', 'REAL_PROPERTY', 'Mortgages and Security Devices', 'Foreclosure > Parties and priorities',
    'Mary bought a small storefront building from Barnabas to run a private Christian bookstore and tutoring studio. To finance the purchase, Mary gave Grace Finance a mortgage on the building. Mary''s deed was properly recorded, but Grace Finance did not record its mortgage. Fourteen months later, Mary borrowed money from Cedar Bank and gave Cedar Bank a mortgage on the same building. Cedar Bank properly recorded its mortgage. Three weeks later, Grace Finance properly recorded its original purchase loan mortgage. Mary later stopped paying both loans. Cedar Bank foreclosed on the building, but it did not name Grace Finance as a party. Stephen bought the building at Cedar Bank''s foreclosure sale without knowing about Grace Finance''s mortgage. Shortly afterward, Grace Finance began its own foreclosure on the building.', 'Mary bought a small storefront building from Barnabas to run a private Christian bookstore and tutoring studio. To finance the purchase, Mary gave Grace Finance a mortgage on the building. Mary''s deed was properly recorded, but Grace Finance did not record its mortgage. Fourteen months later, Mary borrowed money from Cedar Bank and gave Cedar Bank a mortgage on the same building. Cedar Bank properly recorded its mortgage. Three weeks later, Grace Finance properly recorded its original purchase loan mortgage. Mary later stopped paying both loans. Cedar Bank foreclosed on the building, but it did not name Grace Finance as a party. Stephen bought the building at Cedar Bank''s foreclosure sale without knowing about Grace Finance''s mortgage. Shortly afterward, Grace Finance began its own foreclosure on the building.', 'May Grace Finance foreclose its mortgage after Stephen purchased the building at the foreclosure sale?',
