    'After sinkholes damaged a town-owned splash-pad complex, the town locked the gates and stopped using a small concrete apron behind the concession building 28 years ago. Soon afterward, Paul, a retired hymnbook binder, built a small cabin on that apron, kept beehives there, and planted fig trees and vegetables in raised beds. He has lived there continuously since then. This year, the town voted to repair the splash pad and ordered Paul to leave and remove his cabin, hives, and beds. Paul refused, asserting that he had become the owner of the apron by adverse possession. A statute in the jurisdiction conditions ownership by adverse possession on 20 years of continuous, hostile, open, and notorious possession.', 'After sinkholes damaged a town-owned splash-pad complex, the town locked the gates and stopped using a small concrete apron behind the concession building 28 years ago. Soon afterward, Paul, a retired hymnbook binder, built a small cabin on that apron, kept beehives there, and planted fig trees and vegetables in raised beds. He has lived there continuously since then. This year, the town voted to repair the splash pad and ordered Paul to leave and remove his cabin, hives, and beds. Paul refused, asserting that he had become the owner of the apron by adverse possession. A statute in the jurisdiction conditions ownership by adverse possession on 20 years of continuous, hostile, open, and notorious possession.', 'If the town brings a proceeding to eject Paul, what will the outcome most likely turn on?',
