) VALUES (
    '15097_sleeping-apprehension', 'TORTS', 'Intentional Torts', 'Assault',
    'Peter and Daniel are roommates at a Christian study retreat center. One evening, Daniel stays up late to pray and read Scripture. Around midnight, Peter stumbles back to their shared cabin after secretly drinking at a bonfire. Enraged over an earlier argument, Peter grabs a heavy flashlight from the hallway table and kicks open the cabin door, intending to strike Daniel in the head while Daniel prays. Daniel is kneeling with his eyes closed and his back to the door. Just as Peter raises the flashlight, Daniel''s phone buzzes loudly with a call from his mother. Daniel opens his eyes and turns around. Peter immediately lowers the flashlight, shoves it into his backpack, and leaves. The next morning, another retreatant tells Peter that he saw Peter lurking outside the cabin with the flashlight the night before. Daniel, shaken, files a civil suit against Peter for assault.

**A:** Yes, because Peter intended to inflict serious bodily harm on Daniel.

**B:** Yes, because it was reasonable for Daniel to feel afraid after learning what Peter had planned.

**C:** No, because Daniel was unaware of Peter''s presence and intent at the time Peter entered the cabin.

**D:** No, because Peter never made physical contact with Daniel.', 'Peter and Daniel are roommates at a Christian study retreat center. One evening, Daniel stays up late to pray and read Scripture. Around midnight, Peter stumbles back to their shared cabin after secretly drinking at a bonfire. Enraged over an earlier argument, Peter grabs a heavy flashlight from the hallway table and kicks open the cabin door, intending to strike Daniel in the head while Daniel prays. Daniel is kneeling with his eyes closed and his back to the door. Just as Peter raises the flashlight, Daniel''s phone buzzes loudly with a call from his mother. Daniel opens his eyes and turns around. Peter immediately lowers the flashlight, shoves it into his backpack, and leaves. The next morning, another retreatant tells Peter that he saw Peter lurking outside the cabin with the flashlight the night before. Daniel, shaken, files a civil suit against Peter for assault.

**A:** Yes, because Peter intended to inflict serious bodily harm on Daniel.

**B:** Yes, because it was reasonable for Daniel to feel afraid after learning what Peter had planned.

**C:** No, because Daniel was unaware of Peter''s presence and intent at the time Peter entered the cabin.

**D:** No, because Peter never made physical contact with Daniel.', 'Is Daniel likely to prevail?',
