    '15123_christian-bookstore-locked', 'TORTS', 'Intentional Torts', 'False imprisonment',
    'On a Saturday evening after a church conference, Lydia was still inside a Christian bookstore that her pastor had rented for a weekend retreat. She was reading in a back room and did not hear the store''s closing announcement. Timothy, the volunteer coordinator for the retreat, was asked by the pastor to lock up the building for the night. Timothy locked all the exterior doors and left. Lydia discovered she was locked in when she finished her book and tried to leave at 9 p.m. She called her husband, who came and unlocked a side door at 10:45 p.m. Lydia was frustrated and embarrassed by the detention, but suffered no other harm.

