    '15239_auctioneer-tractor', 'TORTS', 'Strict Liability and Products Liability', 'Defenses',
    'Barnabas owns a small woodworking shop where he builds custom furniture. He borrowed money from a local bank and pledged his shop equipment as collateral. When Barnabas defaulted on the loan, the bank foreclosed and hired Timothy, a licensed auctioneer, to sell the equipment at a public auction. Timothy had never sold woodworking equipment before and was hired only for this single estate liquidation. Lydia, a hobbyist woodworker, purchased a table saw at the auction. A few weeks later, while using the saw at her home workshop, a latent defect in the saw''s blade guard caused the guard to retract unexpectedly during operation, severely cutting Lydia''s hand. Lydia sued Timothy in strict products liability. The jurisdiction has not adopted comparative fault in strict liability cases. The result should be for the

**A:** plaintiff, because Timothy sold a defective product that injured the plaintiff.

**B:** defendant, because Timothy is not a commercial seller of woodworking equipment.

**C:** plaintiff, because Timothy failed to inspect the saw for defects before selling it.

**D:** defendant, because Lydia''s own negligence contributed to the accident.', 'Barnabas owns a small woodworking shop where he builds custom furniture. He borrowed money from a local bank and pledged his shop equipment as collateral. When Barnabas defaulted on the loan, the bank foreclosed and hired Timothy, a licensed auctioneer, to sell the equipment at a public auction. Timothy had never sold woodworking equipment before and was hired only for this single estate liquidation. Lydia, a hobbyist woodworker, purchased a table saw at the auction. A few weeks later, while using the saw at her home workshop, a latent defect in the saw''s blade guard caused the guard to retract unexpectedly during operation, severely cutting Lydia''s hand. Lydia sued Timothy in strict products liability. The jurisdiction has not adopted comparative fault in strict liability cases. The result should be for the

