    'Daniel, a 16-year-old student, purchased a Creation Lantern Workshop kit manufactured by Lampstand Learning, Inc., a private Christian homeschool-supply company. The kit taught safe demonstrations about light and color and included mineral powders, a binding solution, and a small alcohol lamp. Daniel invited Lydia, his classmate, to help him with a project. After reading an online survival-craft manual about emergency signal flares and realizing that the kit contained the materials described there, Daniel and Lydia agreed to make a flare. During the project, Daniel carelessly tipped the lit alcohol lamp into a bowl containing materials from the kit. The bowl flared and burned Lydia. The kit was as safe as possible for its educational lantern projects, and its educational benefits exceeded its risks, but it did not warn that its contents could be combined with outside instructions to make dangerous signal flares.', 'Daniel, a 16-year-old student, purchased a Creation Lantern Workshop kit manufactured by Lampstand Learning, Inc., a private Christian homeschool-supply company. The kit taught safe demonstrations about light and color and included mineral powders, a binding solution, and a small alcohol lamp. Daniel invited Lydia, his classmate, to help him with a project. After reading an online survival-craft manual about emergency signal flares and realizing that the kit contained the materials described there, Daniel and Lydia agreed to make a flare. During the project, Daniel carelessly tipped the lit alcohol lamp into a bowl containing materials from the kit. The bowl flared and burned Lydia. The kit was as safe as possible for its educational lantern projects, and its educational benefits exceeded its risks, but it did not warn that its contents could be combined with outside instructions to make dangerous signal flares.', 'In a strict liability suit by Lydia against Lampstand Learning, Lydia will',
