    '17111_parish_newsletter_republication', 'TORTS', 'Defamation', 'Republication and attribution defense',
    'Naomi is the lead Sunday school teacher at a local church school. Mary runs a Christian parenting newsletter that goes out weekly to several hundred subscribers in the area, most of them parents whose children attend the church school. A parent at the church school emailed Mary alleging that Naomi had been stealing from the classroom supply fund, a charge the parent could not substantiate and that was in fact false. Mary had no independent reason to believe the charge was true but, in her next newsletter, repeated the accusation under the heading, "A parent in our school community writes: this teacher has been stealing from the classroom supply fund." Naomi sues Mary for defamation.', 'Naomi is the lead Sunday school teacher at a local church school. Mary runs a Christian parenting newsletter that goes out weekly to several hundred subscribers in the area, most of them parents whose children attend the church school. A parent at the church school emailed Mary alleging that Naomi had been stealing from the classroom supply fund, a charge the parent could not substantiate and that was in fact false. Mary had no independent reason to believe the charge was true but, in her next newsletter, repeated the accusation under the heading, "A parent in our school community writes: this teacher has been stealing from the classroom supply fund." Naomi sues Mary for defamation.', 'Is Mary liable to Naomi as a publisher of the defamatory statement?',
