) VALUES (
    '17956_stewards_heavyheart', 'TORTS', 'Economic torts', 'Malicious prosecution — favorable termination element',
    'Lydia, who runs a small heritage-seed business in Sonoma County, contracted to sell a one-year exclusive on her prized Brandywine tomato seed stock to a wholesale produce distributor run by Paul. When a hard late-spring frost wiped out half the stock, Lydia could not deliver the full exclusive order. Paul promptly sued Lydia for breach of contract in state court. While Paul''s breach suit was still pending, Lydia — believing Paul filed the suit out of spite because she had refused his earlier offer to merge her business into his — filed a separate tort claim against Paul for malicious prosecution, alleging he filed the contract suit without probable cause and with malice. What is Lydia''s strongest problem with her malicious prosecution claim?', 'Lydia, who runs a small heritage-seed business in Sonoma County, contracted to sell a one-year exclusive on her prized Brandywine tomato seed stock to a wholesale produce distributor run by Paul. When a hard late-spring frost wiped out half the stock, Lydia could not deliver the full exclusive order. Paul promptly sued Lydia for breach of contract in state court. While Paul''s breach suit was still pending, Lydia — believing Paul filed the suit out of spite because she had refused his earlier offer to merge her business into his — filed a separate tort claim against Paul for malicious prosecution, alleging he filed the contract suit without probable cause and with malice. What is Lydia''s strongest problem with her malicious prosecution claim?', 'What is Lydia''s strongest problem with her malicious-prosecution claim?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "17956", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "62050403", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
