    'A Christian retreat center in the foothills charged $40 admission to a Saturday women''s ministry day-retreat. For several days, a wooden floorboard on the lodge''s front porch had been rocking loose whenever anyone stepped on it. The retreat center had no inspection schedule for the entrance area. Mary, an attendee, walked onto the porch to enter the lodge and tripped on the loose board, injuring her ankle. What duty did the retreat center owe Mary?', 'A Christian retreat center in the foothills charged $40 admission to a Saturday women''s ministry day-retreat. For several days, a wooden floorboard on the lodge''s front porch had been rocking loose whenever anyone stepped on it. The retreat center had no inspection schedule for the entrance area. Mary, an attendee, walked onto the porch to enter the lodge and tripped on the loose board, injuring her ankle. What duty did the retreat center owe Mary?', 'What duty did the retreat center owe Mary?',
