    'A Christian academy operates a school-bus service for its athletic program. Lydia, an employee of the academy, was driving a school bus to a Saturday basketball game at another Christian school when the bus collided with a car driven by Paul. Hannah, a parent volunteer riding on the bus to help supervise the team, was injured. The court held the academy, Lydia, and Paul jointly and severally liable for Hannah''s damages, and the jury found Hannah to be free from fault. In enforcing the judgment, what portion of her damages is Hannah entitled to collect from the employee, Lydia?', 'A Christian academy operates a school-bus service for its athletic program. Lydia, an employee of the academy, was driving a school bus to a Saturday basketball game at another Christian school when the bus collided with a car driven by Paul. Hannah, a parent volunteer riding on the bus to help supervise the team, was injured. The court held the academy, Lydia, and Paul jointly and severally liable for Hannah''s damages, and the jury found Hannah to be free from fault. In enforcing the judgment, what portion of her damages is Hannah entitled to collect from the employee, Lydia?', 'In enforcing the judgment, what portion of her damages is Hannah entitled to collect from the employee, Lydia?',
