    '18287_manger_cradle_collapse', 'TORTS', 'Negligence', 'Breach — Res ipsa loquitur (rented equipment; plaintiff alteration as competing cause)',
    'Mary, the drama-ministry director at a small church, rented a hand-carved olive-wood manger cradle from Daniel, a Christian craftsman who runs a small home-based Nativity-prop rental business, to use as the centerpiece of the church''s outdoor Living Nativity display. The rental agreement was a standard weekly rental at a normal fee. Mary took the cradle home a week before Christmas Eve. To thread a hidden low-voltage LED light cord through the base so the display would not show wires, Mary drilled four small pilot holes in the cradle''s bottom plate. On Christmas Eve, while Mary was setting the carved baby-Jesus figurine on the cradle, the cradle''s right side rail snapped away from the base and the figurine fell. Mary cannot show whether the failure came from a hidden joint defect in Daniel''s carving or from Mary''s drilled pilot holes.', 'Mary, the drama-ministry director at a small church, rented a hand-carved olive-wood manger cradle from Daniel, a Christian craftsman who runs a small home-based Nativity-prop rental business, to use as the centerpiece of the church''s outdoor Living Nativity display. The rental agreement was a standard weekly rental at a normal fee. Mary took the cradle home a week before Christmas Eve. To thread a hidden low-voltage LED light cord through the base so the display would not show wires, Mary drilled four small pilot holes in the cradle''s bottom plate. On Christmas Eve, while Mary was setting the carved baby-Jesus figurine on the cradle, the cradle''s right side rail snapped away from the base and the figurine fell. Mary cannot show whether the failure came from a hidden joint defect in Daniel''s carving or from Mary''s drilled pilot holes.', 'What is the best res ipsa loquitur analysis of Mary''s res ipsa claim against Daniel?',
    NULL, 'draft', 'c3_transformed', 1, '{"source_qid": "18287", "schema_variant": "transformed_v1", "outline_code": "61020304", "transformed": true, "c3_confidence": "ANCHOR_ASSISTED", "c3_verdict": "PASS"}'
