    '20979_lydia-lotion', 'TORTS', 'Strict Liability and Products Liability', 'Implied warranties',
    'Lydia is a licensed cosmetologist who operates a small skincare business from her home. She purchased a bulk container of hand lotion from a national manufacturer to resell to her clients individually. One of her clients, Martha, applied the lotion to her hands and developed a severe skin rash. Martha asserts a claim against the manufacturer on the ground that the lotion was not merchantable.

(A) The retailer from whom Lydia purchased the lotion bought it from an independent distributor that purchased it from the manufacturer.

(B) Before marketing the lotion, the manufacturer conducted reasonable testing to determine whether the product would cause irritation to normal skin.

(C) Prior to manufacturing and marketing the lotion, the manufacturer received approval for its sale from the federal Food and Drug Administration.

(D) Martha''s allergic reaction was the only such reaction that ever occurred among users of the lotion.', 'Lydia is a licensed cosmetologist who operates a small skincare business from her home. She purchased a bulk container of hand lotion from a national manufacturer to resell to her clients individually. One of her clients, Martha, applied the lotion to her hands and developed a severe skin rash. Martha asserts a claim against the manufacturer on the ground that the lotion was not merchantable.

(A) The retailer from whom Lydia purchased the lotion bought it from an independent distributor that purchased it from the manufacturer.

(B) Before marketing the lotion, the manufacturer conducted reasonable testing to determine whether the product would cause irritation to normal skin.

(C) Prior to manufacturing and marketing the lotion, the manufacturer received approval for its sale from the federal Food and Drug Administration.

(D) Martha''s allergic reaction was the only such reaction that ever occurred among users of the lotion.', 'Which of the following additional facts or inferences, if it were the only one true, would provide the manufacturer with its most effective defense?',
